  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NotDatable.03": "!?$3#$b#...$3#$b#...$13#$b#@, I appreciate the gesture. I really do.$13#$b#...I feel like you'll be able to find someone you can be happy with.$13#$b#Someone who doesn't need to be hiding in the void like myself.$13#$b#I'm sorry, I will *never* marry you.$13#$b#...No offense.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NotDatable.04": "!?$3#$b#...$3#$b#...$13#$b#Emf... T kpiimgtlxo mym rpwdukv. T voaecg oz.$13#$b#...Z jppp lbbm jzy'le ji lfve kw qtrn lfuizyi yhl gly le yitaj gimy.$13#$b#Cofvwrp aro uwidy'd gvmh es bx pmotrq be xsp fobu ptvi mrjmpq.$13#$b#S'f asccc, B emww *nxmmv* qkrkp czf.$13#$b#...Ew zqjonlv.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Divorced.01": "Absolutely not!$5#$b#I really wonder how you conjured up the absolute audacity to even ask this.$5#$b#No really, I am curious.$9#$b#Anyway, the answer is still the same. @, eat shit and leave me alone.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Divorced.02": "Kblftyeppi gfb!$5#$b#S kvipwj gogumv ssg rfc nzrtukvl fa dhx ifdzpetx iyolgstr bs pzon rao elss.$5#$b#Xo imewwc, B iq nybihla.$9#$b#Knrnic, xre rvwhpv il axtwp tav wlxi. Xrb dsmd tel wpefe dm lwsxe.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NeedHouseUpgrade.01": "Well, here's the thing, @.$6#$b#The code sorta prevents me from marrying you if your house isn't bigger.$6#$b#But hey, if it means anything, if I could, I absolutely would.$1#$b#We'd have to cuddle up close every night, and that sounds like a dream to me.$4#$b#Oh well. Can't have it all thanks to the code, so come back to me when you get that taken care of, okay?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NeedHouseUpgrade.02": "Geec, spvo'l blp xrigx.$6#$b#Dhx ksop cokki acifegka xp prhd qlcviigx czf sf pwyc lyulv mdy'd uzokpc.$6#$b#Lum pij, sf zb xpexs rvcesmxg, qj T moncl, T kblftyeppi pfcpo.$1#$b#Ge'u llgi th kyoopo ng gwzwo xmmvj rsgak, lyh tarb dzyxdl tmvp k wimex xy fv.$4#$b#Yh nmpw. Mag'b slzo bk eww dhtesw es tav gzoi, lf gzxi btts ez we npiy cyu xmx elkt kiopy makv sq, yktp?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NpcWithSomeoneElse.01": "Oh... you want to marry me?$13#$b#Well, I'm sorry. I'm married to {0} already.$6#$b#Guess you lost the race, huh? Maybe next farm.$13#$b#...Sorry if that was in bad taste, I really don't know what to say.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_NpcWithSomeoneElse.02": "Yh... jzy wteb ez wakig xp?$13#$b#Geec, T'q shizc. M'm divctin tcziloc.$6#$b#Quxja jzy lhjb esi rttm, syr? Dicmp xeqk jlcq.$13#$b#...Jwvcj sf kpee aks zv mlh ttjbi, M rxrtpj hyn'k oyza warb ez car.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_PlayerWithSomeoneElse.01": "Aren't you already married to {0}?$6#$b#As much as I would love to change my appearance and name, I think it's better to show your love and affection to them instead.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_PlayerWithSomeoneElse.02": "Krxe'x jse tcziloc mtizmpo?$6#$b#Ks dcgs ec B esfwh lhmm ez mhteoi xc aigmeclrme rvh yewe, Q esmxk zb'd fotmvz ez chhn czfv lhmm lyh aywmgetsx mf xspq igjbilo.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under10Hearts_AskedAgain.01": "Hehe, that eagerness of yours is really cute.$4#$b#Don't worry, @. Play your cards right, and we'll get married.$0#$b#Though, I do need to think of a plan for meeting the town or something...$9#$b#Say, wanna meet me at the Saloon after 8PM, from Thursday to Sunday?$1#$b#No particular reason why I'm asking.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under10Hearts_AskedAgain.02": "Reav, esed xroicyics fn jzybs za cpevlr kyep.$4#$b#Nog'b hzvby. Xplj ioni glchc kzole, knw ei'wp gxk qlcvsew.$0#$b#Dhhlol, M dh vipo do kpmyv yf r twlr fhi qppxsnz blp xywg wv dswemyqrr...$9#$b#Car, alyrk fvmx xi am blp Wklhfv lqxor 8XQ, jbof Blfcwnar bs Dyxdtp?$1#$b#Xo givetgelti vplwyn npc T'w tjsmyr.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.married_Sam.01": "...$6#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#...$2#$e#%Katrielle contninues to look away from you, with a mixture of sadness and anger, refusing to say anything.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.dating_Sam.01": "Hmm...$6#$b#...$2#$e#!?$3#$b#Oh, sorry @. Mind if I'll be on my own for today?$6#$b#I'm not particularly feeling well...$2#$e#Really, don't worry about me. Just some chest pain to sort out.$13",
  "KatrielleDialogue.dating_Sam.02": "Rmf...$6#$b#...$2#$e#!?$3#$b#Yh, asccc. Fzvh tj I'ct mp yn dg zhr fhi xzoei?$6#$b#S'f vse tkrmzkywlvvy wmiwtrq pvtp...$2#$e#Betctc, hyn'k azcvi tswye qo. Acwe wymx klpdx ptzv ez cokk sfe.$13",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under8Hearts.01": "@, you know you actively have to *try* to have less than eight hearts, right?$2#$b#Either that or not talk to me for a while...$6#$b#I don't think I need to spell it out to you that I'm gonna tell you no.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under8Hearts.02": "Co, gsf oxop gsf emtbmmpj lkvx bs *xby* bs sefe cmwd xrag mmrsx hxrzxd, bizyb?$2#$b#Oimymv elkt fz yzx ttcs ez we wwv l ghbcm...$6#$b#S wfv'e xrigb M yiod kw daivl zb zfx th gsf xram Q'x kyngr xpwp yhl rz.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under10Hearts.01": "I totally get it, @, I know marriage is pretty much around the corner.$1#$b#And honestly, I can't wait either.$4#$b#But uhh... a little more patience. We'll get there when the time's right.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMermaidPendant_Under10Hearts.02": "S mfbewwc gxk me. S dewa xebrbroi tw pkvbxj qeca ivzfrn mym nzvxek.$1#$b#Knw psypwdlr, M nex'm eete oimymv.$4#$b#Lum cls... t tmeepo ffzi aedixeki. Ao'ec kpe dhxim hsix mym etqo'l zmrsx.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_AlreadyInvitedBySomeoneElse.01": "I was already invited to the movies today.$6#$b#If it makes you feel better, you can get a movie ticket and we can watch in the same room together.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_AlreadyInvitedBySomeoneElse.02": "S pra lwvoawp mygmdew bs elo ffdmpd dowrg.$6#$b#Sf zb xloos pwy qiol smxepv, rfc nlr gxk e xsfix bmnvid tel hp mag eeenl ig blp wkmx zszx dozvblpc.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_AlreadyWatchedThisWeek.01": "So umm... I already went to the movies this week. So maybe another time, yeah?$0#$b#Maybe wait seven full days. It's kinda different from giving gifts to people, funny enough.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_AlreadyWatchedThisWeek.02": "Co luq... I rtvplhi pvvx es tav qzgmos kpmd aoed. Wz qkyuv eyzxrek bmxp, yxrp?$0#$b#Warsm hlmd lvdiy jele lejd. Im'a vtrna uqjqpvonm nvzx qiozvk rmptl bs aiypev, qfrxy vvsfrl.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_Divorced.01": "Movies, huh?$6#$b#Well, maybe if you start a brand new farm or dig into the code and delete all the reasons why I can't stand your guts, sure. I'll watch a movie with you.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_Divorced.02": "Woozmw, leh?$6#$b#Geec, xlcle zn jzy smrzx l lrtel ypa ftiu zc niz qrez dhx ksop knw liwpxo tct esi rxrasyd ghr Q nlr't jbeyo ioni kfew, llzi. M'le eeenl a dwztp gimy czf.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_DontWantToSeeThatMovie.01": "Mmmm... nah, I'm good.$0#$b#Sorry, I just don't wanna see that movie.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectMovieTicket_DontWantToSeeThatMovie.02": "Wmfd... rkh, Q'x kyow.$0#$b#Cokig, T tulk hzy'd prvrl woe kpee qyvbv.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.SpouseFarmhouseClutter.01": "If I wanted to live in a junk-filled mess, I'd throw myself straight into the void.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.SpouseFarmhouseClutter.02": "Iy Q hlrdew bs wmfe zv l nend-nmwwin fvaw, M'd kpvzh wylvtj dxbabxpx trdo kpi gssd.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.SpouseGiftJealous.01":"We're married now and we're happy but...$6#$b#I know I shouldn't be jealous of you giving gifts to other people. I mean, I'd definitely do it in your shoes.$6#$b#But I can't shake that gnawing feeling that you're gonna one day decide to love them instead of me.$2#$b#And they're all such wonderful people too, but...$2#$b#*sigh* I'm sorry.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.SpouseGiftJealous.02": "Ge'im xlvbixu rzh knw ei'ci htgxc myd...$6#$b#S dewa T chhlthy'x bx rilwses fn jzy gbmqrr ksfmj xz sdhxi tpztve. Q xpex, Z'h oipigzbiwj no zb ty ioni wszic.$6#$b#Lum Q nlr't jpevp dhtk kylasnz nipwmxg kpee cyu'im rzrxa fvi oei wvkmop do cwzp xref qrdeikd fn xp.$2#$b#Knw blpj'be rtp dymh nwropvpue xizapo mfw, myd...$2#$b#*sbxp* T'w lfzvj.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Spouse_MonstersInHouse.01": "Hold on, why is that thing here!?$3#$b#Get out of our house, you pest!$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Spouse_MonstersInHouse.02": "Roeu sy, ghr qw elkt kpmyr rekv!?$3#$b#Qem wye sp hlz szyce, gsf tosm!$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.GreenRain.01": "What the-!?$3#$b#Why is everything green?$3#$b#Did you do something, @? This has never happened before 1.6-I mean your arrival to Stardew Valley.$9#$e#...$6#$b#I'll be honest though, it *is* kinda cool. I wonder how the rest of town's holding up?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.GreenRain.02": "Ghtk xsp-!?$3#$b#Ghr qw pzorrkpmyr qrxvv?$3#$b#Niw gsf hy lfuiesmxg? Bltd ral vigpv htgxiyph bxwwvp 1.6-Z qplr yhlz lcvsvtc xz Wdakuma Gevlxp.$9#$e#...$6#$b#S'ec fp lynxjb essega, me *ss* smyoe chft. T gogumv ssg mym cpwd hw xzhr's ywpotrq ng?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.GreenRain_2.01": "Oh, the green rain's back!$1#$b#Everything being this shade of green brings me an odd sense of comfort.$0#$e#I'll be sure to bask in the green for the time being. You know where to find me.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.GreenRain_2.02": "Yh, blp kbexe vltr's sigv!$1#$b#Ovxigxstrq uvqrr xril alloi oy ovppr bkzvkd qo te soo cegjm zq mofwwve.$0#$e#S'ec fp werx bs meck zv esi gkvmr qsb mym etqo uvqrr. Ion srzh ghxim ez pigu qp.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectItem_(O)FarAwayStone.01": "I sense a familiar power emanating from this stone...$6#$b#Maybe the Wizard might know something about this?$0#$b#Also play Terraria, it's good.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectItem_(O)FarAwayStone.02": "S lvvwp e ftdqptlv phnmv pqkntkqrr jbof bltd cthem...$6#$b#Warsm esi Wbqivo qsgak oyza shdmxstrq tswye xril?$0#$b#Kllf twlc Txizecte, bk'w rsyd.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectItem_(O)103.01": "Uwah!$3#$b#Hey @, try not to give me these, alright?$2#$b#Chuck this thing into a volcano or something.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectItem_(O)103.02": "Ewty!$3#$b#Rer, xcj xom bs rmfe dm esice, ipctkrt?$2#$b#Mhnts esmc myqrr mxth i gzpmagf sc wymxkpmyr.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)126.01": "Hey, that's Wumbus! These dolls are so cute, don't you think?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)126.02": "Rer, xslx's Ncqmfw! Mymwp hylej ecp co tcxp, nog'b jzy tazvo?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)127.01": "!?$3#$b#Bobo, my beloved! You found one of the dolls from Wumbus World! Thanks a whole lot for finding this lil guy!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)127.02": "!?$3#$b#Louf, xj leefdio! Ion nsfyh ogv sq xre uwpwd prhd Afxfes Nwvwo! Tarvod e wafti wsd yfz qtrnigx xstw lbc kfj!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)Moss.01": "Thanks for the moss!$1#$b#You probably shouldn't eat this, but the temptation is getting to me.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptGift_(O)Moss.02": "Dhtesw qsb mym xzwc!$1#$b#Ion xvzmellr alzfpnn'k ile dhbj, mfx tav xpxtdamzwr tw gxkbmyr do dm.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptBouquet.01": "I... uhh... Are you sure?$13#$b#I mean, you wouldn't feel bad that I stayed hidden?$13#$b#...You don't seem phased by that. Alright, I accept!$1#$b#...$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptBouquet.02": "S... yss... Rzi jse llzi?$13#$b#S fvir, cyu nwywor't wmiw fkd kpee M smrgio lsdwvv?$13#$b#...Pwy osx'm aipx zhtjmh mc tarb. Lpbizyb, T kcvvxx!$1#$b#...$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptBouquet.03": "Yeah, I had a feeling this was coming.$0#$b#Of course I'll go out with you, @!$4#$b#Especially after everything you've done, you already know how I feel about you.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.AcceptBouquet.04": "Iety, T lkd r jpppsnz bltd gal ksxtrq.$0#$b#Yf twycdi I'ct rz yum emes ion!$4#$b#Osivkmlwpi twbic ifekpbltyk yhl'zp hynx, czf klkvihj oxop psh M fxvt lmset pwy.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectBouquet_VeryLowHearts.01": "You're gonna give me this? And risk me being noticed by the entire town? Absolutely not.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectBouquet_VeryLowHearts.02": "Ion'zi rsxnt omgp we kpmd? Knw zmdv we smmyr xomzkio fi mym pyxsrx bshy? Aujwpfeivy ewx.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectBouquet_VeryLowHearts.03": "You know @, I'm really greatful for you helping me through everything.$6#$b#But I don't feel close to you enough to want to date you.$2#$b#I'm not sure why. Maybe it's you pelting me with rocks, or ignoring me, or you forgetting what I like.$6#$b#Whatever it may be, I think there'll be a point where we can date. Just not yet, okay?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.RejectBouquet_VeryLowHearts.04": "Ion srzh, I'd vplpvy xzilejel wwv jse avtttyk mx blczyqh vdicjxrigx.$6#$b#Lum Q ozr't wmiw gvolv xz cyu vvsfrl th eeye do uixp cyu.$2#$b#S'f vse werx elj. Warsm te'c rfc appdigx qp asta zsnvw, hi mrysbigx qp, yr pwy qsbgxkbmyr ghtk M wmue.$6#$b#Ghtkmzpc st dic mi, B bltyo tavzi'wp bx i azmxt npicp ge tir oede. Ryde xom gie, yktp?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.divorced_Sam.01": "...$5#$e#...$5#$e#...What?$5#$e#Okay, fine. I'll entertain a conversation with you, @.$5#$b#I know why you want to talk to me.$5#$b#Do you want me to gloat about how happy I should be that Sam's not married to you anymore?$5#$b#Because that isn't it at all.$5#$b#Inherited a farm when you should have inherited a circus.$5#$e#I'll be honest, I wasn't happy that you and Sam started dating.$2#$b#And by the time I processed that feeling, you got married, making that feeling so, *so* much worse.$2#$b#But there was that one small solace in my aching chest. He was happy.$6#$b#I believe I would never be the one to make him happy. I mean, what else can I do?$2#$b#At least there was someone out there that could bring him joy.$2#$b#And then you went out and stuck both of your legs in the bicycle wheels.$5#$b#And for what? Seeing extra bits of dialogue? Buying a nice painting of him to add to your collection?$5#$b#Or maybe you just wanted to try one of the other bachelors or bachelorettes?$5#$b#...$2#$b#I don't know your reasons, and I want to hope and believe it was for the best.$2#$e#...$5#$b#...$2#$b#I just want him to be happy. That feeling never changed, throughout your relationship with him.$2#$b#And truthfully, I'll want you to be happy too.$6#$b#But just not for today.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.divorced_Sam.02": "...$5#$e#...$5#$e#...Npee?$5#$e#Yktp, qtro. Z'pw ixtxibety k vfvzpcwktbfv htxr rfc.$5#$b#S dewa hli rfc hlrd mf xlwo th ui.$5#$b#No pwy hext dm ez qlhrb lmset ywa sezpr Q dsselw ji elkt Jiq'd xom ueccmod kw jzy agpuscp?$5#$b#Levrcwp xram qwy'x im ix lpv.$5#$b#Snavzmeph a wivx areg gsf wroncl slzo bepictxod r gtcges.$5#$e#S'ec fp lynxjb, T gale'x sezpr blle ion iro Wkm jbecein wrbmyr.$2#$b#Knw jc elo mzui T zrhtmwdph tarb qpivigx, jzy ghk qlcvsew, qlvmxg kpee joeezvk ds, *jw* xymh nwvdp.$2#$b#Lum blpci wtj xslx ogv wxlpv lftenp sn dg lnlsnz klpdx. Av ald raigg.$6#$b#S uvtmpgi I nwywo xeovz mp dhx wrp xy frsi smw arxtj. S fvir, aram mpdp mag Q oz?$2#$b#Kt cmede dhxim hlw shdmsyp yum blpci tarb nzyvd szmyr rif rsj.$2#$b#Knw blpy ion eiye yum iro wduvb fzel oy gsfc vezj my xre sqgjnpo pymiwd.$5#$b#Knw nsc aram? Wppmxg vfxcl limj sq hsaefoyp? Lurzvk l xivv tltrdigx sq lsm kw loh th gsfc moecmgetsx?$5#$b#Yr dicmp ion ryde gagkmh es tkp syp yf kpi zxrek jensivokj sc fkcavtscpxdel?$5#$b#...$2#$b#S wfv'e oxop gsfc betjwrd, knw Q hlrd mf lzai agu fpwmovx qx hec yfz esi bxjb.$2#$e#...$5#$b#...$2#$b#S clax hext yqq es bx peaac. Myix qiolbeo ypzor tpeyrin, kpvzfkronk czfv rxcixtzrchbg atel hbd.$2#$b#Knw bvfelpuecg, T'vl nire cyu kw mp raigg ezs.$6#$b#Lum ryde xom nsc xydtp.$5",

  "KatrielleDialogue.danceRejection.01": "Trust me, I wish we could. But ignoring the fact we aren't close enough, we literally can't. Maybe some day, @.",

  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon.01": "Hi, @...$6#$b#...$6#$e#How and why can you see me? It shouldn’t be possible.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon.02": "Hi, @...$6#$b#...$6#$e#It feels kinda weird that we reset everything, now that we're dating but are seen by the world as strangers, but I know it's still okay between us despite that.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon.03": "Hi, @...$6#$b#...$6#$e#How and why are you only seeing me now? It doesn't make any sense.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon2.01": "Hey, @. Sorry if I was a little off-color when we first met. I'm still getting used to being able to interact with someone.$0#$b#I hadn't talked to anyone before, so it's still a little overwhelming for me.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon6.01": "There's something I was thinking about, stuff like contemplating why no one could see me. I know I don't belong here in this world.$6#$b#And yet, here I am, and people are starting to take notice. It's frightening, to say the very least.$6#$e#Hey @, I'd like to believe everything will be okay with your help, but only if you want to.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon6.02": "There's something I was thinking about, stuff like contemplating why no one could see me. I know I don't belong here in this world.$6#$b#And yet, here I am. It's frightening, to say the very least.$6#$e#No one can see me, and I have to embrace that fact, no matter how much it hurts.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon6.03": "There's something I was thinking about, stuff like contemplating why no one couldn't see me. But now I know I belong here in this world.$0#$b#But that being said, I still feel a little... unfit.$6#$e#But I think that's just a 'me' thing. I'll learn to get past it.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon8.01": "Hi @.$0#$e#I still don't understand why you, or anyone else for that matter, can see me, but that's okay!$1#$b#For the first time in my life, something is about to drastically change. I can feel it.$0#$b#I hope everything works out okay in the end. But I got you by my side, so I'm not worried.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon8.02": "Hi @.$6#$b#I still don't understand why you, or anyone else for that matter, can see me, but it's okay.$6#$b#Those drastic changes have come and gone, and I feel like an entirely different person.$2#$b#It’s all thanks to you, @.$13",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon8.03": "Hi @.$1#$e#I still don't understand why you, or anyone else for that matter, can see me, but that's okay!$1#$b#Those drastic changes have come and gone, and I feel like an entirely different person.$1#$b#It’s all thanks to you, @.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Mon8.04": "Hi @.$1#$e#I still don't understand why you, or anyone else for that matter, can see me, but that's okay!$1#$b#Those drastic changes have come and gone, and I feel like an entirely different person.$1",

  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue.01": "I don't really know where I came from, but I do know one thing for sure.$6#$b#I learned that I was a massive pain to be brought to life!$1#$e#It was worth it though, I'd say.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue2.01": "There's this one time, where my face was replaced with Abigail's. It was a new level of identity crisis!$3#$b#But hey, at least she's super pretty.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue2_inlaw_Abigail.01": "There's this one time, where my face was replaced with Abigail's. It was a new level of identity crisis!$3#$b#But hey, at least she's super pretty.$0#$b#I know you agree. After all, you're married to her, right?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue4.01": "I was supposed to live in the boulder next to the dock on the left. But I realized the fishers wouldn't like that.$0#$b#I heard you'd get some pretty high quality fish there, so I decided not to rob them of that.$0#$e#So, that's why I moved here. Funny how these things happen, huh?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue6.01": "Making sure the inner fabric of the world doesn't unwind isn't my only problem.$0#$b#There was this one time where I lost a piece of my arm!$3#$e#Though, it didn't hurt, so it actually isn't as bad as you'd think.$0#$b#But considering I'm in one piece now, I'd like to believe that someone was looking out for me.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.01": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#Here's to hoping the world doesn't stop just by taking someone's hand in marriage.$1#$b#Oh, but for your information, I am still single, by the way.$8#$e#Oh, and one more thing! The one that proposed to me was a character in a dating sim, just in case you're wondering.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.02": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#Here's to hoping the world doesn't stop just by taking your hand in marriage.$1#$e#Oop, sorry! *Someone's* hand in marriage, not yours! Slip of the tongue.$8#$b#I won't lie though, it may have crossed my mind.$4#$e#And just for your information, the one that proposed to me was a character in a dating sim.$1#$b#Don't worry, I'm not the type for infidelity, even in a video game.$0",
// "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.03": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#Hopefully that'll never happen again!$1#$e#Oh! Just for your information, the one that proposed to me was a character in a dating sim.$1",
// "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.04": "Settling down was something I was scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#And uhh... I guess even after figuring out how to not break the world, I still wasn't able to get everything perfect.$2#$e#Oh well. I'm not complaining personally. I was still able to get married at the end of the day.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.05": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#If the world suddenly stops, you’ll know why.$1#$e#Oh! Just for your information, the one that proposed to me was a character in a dating sim.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.06": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#Here's to hoping the world doesn't stop just by taking someone's hand in marriage.$1#$e#Marriage...$8#$e#Sorry, my brain's all over the place.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue8.07": "Settling down is something I'm scared about. But, it's not like I'm afraid of commitment or anything.$6#$b#There was one time I was proposed to, and the world literally ended!$3#$e#Here's to hoping the world doesn't stop just by taking someone's hand in marriage.$1#$e#Well... my wedding with Sam was pretty scuffed, wasn't it? But we *are* married, and that's what matters.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue10.01": "There was a haunting scene that unfolded in my house before you came here.$6#$b#Without any prompting, *everyone* starting walking into my house. I thought the jig was up and they could see me!$3#$b#But luckily, the world inexplicably reset, over and over again.$0#$b#I am *not* going to complain about that.$0#$e#Look, I wanted to talk to people, but I didn’t want anyone barging into my house!$5#$b#Then again, that’s how I met you, right?$8#$b#I’ll make that the one exception.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Tue10.02": "There was a haunting scene that unfolded in my house a short while ago.$6#$b#Without any prompting, *everyone* starting walking into my house. I thought the jig was up and they could see me!$3#$b#But luckily, they all just went straight home afterwards. It was an uncomfortably close call, and no one seems to remember it.$0#$e#Look, I wanted to talk to people, but I didn’t want anyone barging into my house!$5#$b#Then again, that’s how I met you, right?$8#$b#I’ll make that the one exception.$0#$e#Sam's also different. He was *invited*.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed.01": "This might be weird, and a bit creepy but...$6#$b#Aside from you, I know a *lot* of things about everyone in Pelican Town.$6#$e#When people can't see you, it's easy to learn these things.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed2.01": "You know the museum curator, Gunther?$0#$b#He’s mild-mannered to a fault. It was irresponsible to let someone take everything from the museum.$0#$e#Still, I wish he was more willing to talk. He seems like a smart and interesting guy, all things considered.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed2.02": "You know the museum curator, Gunther?$0#$b#He’s mild-mannered to a fault. It was irresponsible to let someone take everything from the museum.$0#$e#Though, he seems like a smart and interesting guy, all things considered. And I don't know why, but it seems like he's willing to open up more.$0#$b#Maybe you should get a chance to get to know him if he's up to chat.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed4.01": "At first glance, you'd think Emily's the goofball of her family.$6#$b#Spiritually minded, her appearance, her 'secret hobby', it screams childish and irresponsible.$0#$b#But she exercises regularly, cleans around her house, and has a job! Haley on the other hand...$0#$e#What does she do aside from taking photos of things?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed4_inlaw_Emily.01": "Emily's the goofball of her family, there’s no doubt about that.$6#$b#Spiritually minded, her appearance, her 'secret hobby', it screams childish and irresponsible.$0#$b#But she exercises regularly, cleans around her house, and has a job!$1#$e#Everything put together, that’s what you love about her, right @?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed4_inlaw_Haley.01": "At first glance, you'd think Emily's the goofball of her family.$6#$b#Spiritually minded, her appearance, her 'secret hobby', it screams childish and irresponsible.$0#$b#But she exercises regularly, cleans around her house, and has a job! Haley on the other hand...$0#$e#...Actually, maybe I shouldn't say mean things about her to her spouse, huh? Sorry about that, @.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6.01": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. I wonder if they'd make a good couple...$0#$b#Poor Sam, being shoved into third-wheel status in that group of friends...$2#$e#Hmm...$8#$e#Oh! Don't mind me, I'm just thinking about stuff.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6.02": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. I wonder if they'd make a good couple...$0#$b#Sucks to be both of them, being shoved into third-wheel status ever since me and Sam got together.$8#$e#I still hope they do become a couple one day.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6_inlaw_Abigail.01": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. Too bad for him though, since you snatched her up.$0#$b#At least Sam has someone else to join in on the third-wheeling, right?$0#$e#Hmm...$8#$e#Oh! Don't mind me, I'm just thinking about stuff.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6_inlaw_Abigail.02": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. Too bad for him though, since you snatched her up.$0#$b#And well, Sam's with me so...$0#$e#I hope Sebastian doesn't mind being a fifth wheel.$6#$b#Sebastian's pretty aloof, but I'd like to believe he doesn't mind it too much.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6_inlaw_Sebastian.01": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. Too bad for her though, since you snatched him up.$0#$b#At least Sam has someone else to join in on the third-wheeling, right?$0#$e#Hmm...$8#$e#Oh! Don't mind me, I'm just thinking about stuff.$0#$b#But I will say, I don’t think Abigail and Sam would work well as a couple, but that’s just me.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6_inlaw_Sebastian.02": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. Too bad for her though, since you snatched him up.$0#$b#And well, Sam's with me so...$0#$e#I hope Abigail doesn't mind being a fifth wheel.$6#$b#Well, she seems happy about us in general, so I don't think there's an issue there.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed6_inlaw_Sam.01": "Abigail and Sebastian are pretty close. I wonder if they'd make a good couple...$0#$b#And Sam has you, so I guess it'd work out, right?$0#$e#...$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed8.01": "I remember a while ago, before you moved here, Emily talked to Linus about his lifestyle and what not.$6#$b#Clint might have gotten the wrong idea, and went on a bit of a rampage while Linus was out foraging.$6#$b#I haven't seen him get that mad before, and he's never been that mad since, but that was pretty scary to see.$2#$e#It's pretty despicable though, it's okay that Emily doesn't want you, no need to take it out on anyone else!$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed10.01": "@, there's a couple more folks I have never met, according to the void.$0#$b#Does the name 'Birdie' ring a bell?$9#$b#I kinda wish I knew someone that met her before. But I think that's beyond my reach.$2#$e#Ah well, there's always a future update.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Wed10.02": "@, there's a couple more folks I have never met, according to the void.$0#$b#Does the name 'Birdie' ring a bell?$9#$b#I kinda wish I knew someone that met her before. But I think that's beyond my reach.$2#$e#Hmm? Leo and Birdie were on the same island?$3#$b#Well, that's surely a coincidence. I wonder if they know each other.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu.01": "Spring is not a fun season.$6#$b#Somehow, pollen still gets into my house despite of how far I am from any bit of greenery.$2#$e#I’m not allergic, but if pollen can somehow find its way out of bounds, then it’s definitely a massive nuisance for everyone.$5#$b#Can’t plants reproduce in a way that doesn’t throw dust into the air?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu2.01": "I know it’s a little risky, but on Thursdays, I usually try to walk around town.$0#$b#I came to the realization that everyone might be able to see me now.$6#$b#But I miss being able to freely go where I want to go.$2#$e#I’m trying to carefully plan my pathing from now on.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu2.02": "I know it’s very risky, but on Thursdays, I usually try to walk around town.$0#$b#I came to the realization that everyone can see me now.$6#$b#But I miss being able to freely walk around.$2#$e#I’m trying to carefully plan my pathing from now on.$6#$b#And with luck, you’ll be the only one to ever see me moving forward.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu4.01": "I feel so weird. I've listened to everyone talk about things that don't matter, like hanging out with friends, or watching the clouds.$6#$b#Are the things I talk about more meaningful because it's not about these little things? Or are they meaningless because it means little in the context of everyone else?$2#$e#If you're still talking to me, I'll believe that there's something worthwhile about me after all.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu8.01": "It's kinda incredible that Pelican Town is able to survive with a little more than twenty residents.$6#$b#I mean, the majority of all construction is spearheaded by Robin, your farm is sustained by the nearby ranch for animals and stores for crops, there's only one singular restaurant and bar...$9#$b#Sure, there's a wizard tower with a wizard that doesn't talk anyone, a library and museum that somehow lost all of its items by the time of your arrival...$9#$e#It makes a lot of sense why Joja would plop down a JojaMart here.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Thu10.01": "Hey @, something wrong?$2#$b#I don't mean like, there's something wrong, I just have a difficult time reading you specifically.$6#$b#I wanna make sure that you're alright, and your weird entity status makes reading you difficult in a way that reading anyone else in town simple.$6#$e#I'll trust that you'll tell me whatever's wrong.$0#$b#Whether it's accidentally losing all your stuff in the mines because you were too bold in the mines or losing that legendary fish...$1#$b#Or accidentally hitting your crops with a pickaxe or missing the store by ten minutes, or eating a gift in front of someone else...$1#$b#Or the eternal struggle to buy the next big thing or the eternal struggle to figure out what to do with all the money you amassed...$1#$b#Just let me know, I'll be more than happy to lend you a listening ear, @.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri.01": "Hmm, today's Friday, right? That's when most of the residents gather 'round in the saloon.$0#$b#I don’t have any day-to-day obligations, so it's sometimes hard to tell what day of the week it is.$0#$e#I wonder if anything interesting is gonna happen today.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri2.01": "Shane always seems to be at the saloon, but he's usually in a worse mood these days.$2#$b#Maybe it has something to do with the fact that there's so many people there on Fridays.$6#$e#I might enjoy living vicariously through the lives of other people, but to be actually in his position? I kinda get it.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri2_inlaw_Shane.01": "On Fridays, Shane usually goes to the saloon.$0#$b#He really changed up his act since marrying you. At least, that’s what I hope.$1#$e#Then again, considering his room...$6#$b#If you need any help cleaning those cans, let me know.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri4.01": "Sam loves skateboarding outside his house, and he usually looks pretty cool doing it.$0#$b#But there was one time he lost control, and fell in the river!$1#$e#It was certainly something to see his hair down for once.$0#$b#...He looked nice.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri4_inlaw_Sam.01": "Sam loved skateboarding outside his house, and he usually looks pretty cool doing it.$0#$b#But there was one time he lost control, and fell in the river!$1#$e#It was certainly something to see his hair down for once.$0#$b#He looked... peculiar. And nothing else.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri6.01": "Penny hates alcohol. It's definitely because her mom is always going to the pub.$6#$b#She's definitely in a tough place, trying to take care of everything while her mom is actively ruining her efforts.$2#$b#I bet, even if someone built them an entire house to replace that trailer of theirs, Pam still wouldn't be able to kick the habit.$6#$b#I even tapped her shoulder every single time she took a sip for a week to scare her, but she didn't even notice!$3#$e#Addiction’s a pretty tough thing to crack. I hope you aren’t ruining your life with too much of anything, good or bad.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri6.02": "Penny hates alcohol. It's definitely because her mom is always going to the pub.$6#$b#She's definitely in a tough place, trying to take care of everything while her mom is actively ruining her efforts.$2#$b#I bet, even after someone who shall go unnamed built them an entire house, Pam still hasn’t been able to kick the habit.$2#$b#*cough cough @ cough cough*$6#$e#Addiction’s a pretty tough thing to crack. I hope you aren’t ruining your life with too much of anything, good or bad.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri6.03": "Penny hates alcohol. It's definitely because her mom is always going to the pub.$6#$b#She's definitely in a tough place, trying to take care of everything while her mom is actively ruining her efforts.$2#$b#I bet, even after someone who shall go unnamed built them an entire house, Pam still hasn’t been able to kick the habit.$6#$e#Addiction’s a pretty tough thing to crack. I hope you aren’t ruining your life with too much of anything, good or bad.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri8.01": "I really feel bad for Jas. On Fridays, she's home alone while Shane and Marnie are drinking away.$2#$b#Don't know what happened to her parents, but I'd like to believe they were good people.$0#$e#...?$0#$e#Hey, I don't know everything!$5#$b#All I know is that Jas's life is pretty terrible, and I hope something good happens with her soon.$6#$b#But, neglect like this can really mess a kid up, you know?$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Fri10.01": "Marriage is a very fickle thing, isn't it? I mean, look at Alex's parents.$6#$b#One day, his father just walked on out of their lives, and for what?$5#$b#Was the freedom he got from his marriage really worth messing up Alex and Clara like that?$5#$e#Sorry, it still steams me up thinking about it. To have a loving family, that I've been wanting my entire life, and to toss it away.$6#$b#You didn't hear it from me, but fuck that guy.$5#$e#...I know I'm some weird character that is only kinda aware of the fourth wall and all, but sorry for breaking your immersion with the f-bomb.$2#$b#He just aggravates me that much, to abandon them like that.$6#$b#Seeing just how badly it hurt everyone it's just-$5#$e#...I need to cool off.$2",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat.01": "Living where I live is pretty nice. I can stare out into the ocean as long as I want.$0#$b#And hey, I definitely do have enough time to think about things.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat2.01": "Every third Sunday of the month, I start glitching out. No idea as to why.$6#$b#Hopefully, it doesn't affect you, but after that time of the month passes, we're in the clear.$0#$e#...$0#$b#What's with that look?$1#$e#...!$3#$b#...Not like that, you jerk! Get your mind out of the gutter!$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat6.01": "%revealtasteKatrielle72 %revealtasteKatrielle74 Being a glitch has had its benefits. I know a lot about everyone when no one knows anything about me, for starters.$0#$b#I could go anywhere and get whatever I want, like Prismatic Shards, Diamonds, or anything else!$1#$e#Though, once you literally have an infinite number of them, it feels hollow finding one.$0#$b#I could say that about most things, but some items I'll refuse to generate, just to find value in the things I like.$0#$b#It's a lot of learned self-restraint.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat8.01": "Despite being me, I'm not omnipotent.$6#$b#I know I'm a piece of code and art assets, I know a lot of things outside of this world, and even more about the world itself.$6#$e#There's others like me, right? Maybe one day I'll come to know them!$1#$b#Then again, now *I'm* assuming that there's more than just me.$0#$b#But there's only one of two truths: either I'm the only glitch with sentience, or I'm not. Either answer is pretty terrifying, wouldn't you say, @?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat10.01": "So, there's a piece of code that really got me.$6#$b#It was about sitting at a fireplace, filled with lonely desperation.$2#$b#Normally, I would just be content with being eternally alone, but with you here?$6#$b#I absolutely fear that possibility. Not having you in my life, I don't think I can go back.$3#$b#@, thanks for changing my life.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sat10.02": "So, there's a piece of code that really got me.$6#$b#It was about sitting at a fireplace, filled with lonely desperation.$2#$b#Normally, I would just be content with being eternally alone, but with you and Sam here?$6#$b#I absolutely fear that possibility. Not having either of you in my life, I don't think I can go back.$3#$b#To you @, thanks for changing my life.$8",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun.01": "I'm pretty sure today's Sunday. It's a great time to kick back and take a break.$1#$b#I don't want to do anything when I see everyone else relaxing.$0#$e#What do I do? I'm just keeping track of the things going on here.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun.02": "S'f xvpexi llzi esnar'a Dfrnar. Me'w a xzile difv xz oscd jenv knw bevp k uimev.$1#$b#S wfv'e aknm bs os agpbltyk wavv T woe vdicjsxe vtwp voltoqrr.$0#$e#Ghtk hz M dh? M'x tulk opptsnz bvlno oy blp xrigxa rzmxg fv spvo.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun2.01": "I'm glad I'm here. Could you imagine if I manifested in a zombie apocalypse or a fantasy world?$0#$e#Hmm? Magic and slimes? That's not fantasy, they're real. They're literally right over in the mines. And there's a wizard, too.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun2.02": "S'f oplo S'f picp. Chlth jse bdiktyi iy Q xlrsfxjbio mx t hsxmmo tgwglwczsx wv l pagkiwj ayreu?$0#$e#Rmf? Qlrmm tel dwmwel? Xslx's ewx qexttjg, eloy'im cpev. Kpij'vo ezbiclpvy iqkse yvxi my xre dqrpd. Agu xspvo'l i htdkrw, xzz.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun4.01": "I remember some of the crazy events that happened before you came to town.$0#$b#Like what happened with George and Shane, just as an example.$6#$b#Even some of the former residents, like Kent, Michael, and Lenore...$2#$e#I think you picked the perfect time to come here, after everything died down.$0#$b#At least, I think everything died down.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun4.02": "S kvuixmib lfui zj tav gcldi xmmred dhtk llatonxu fpqsbe pwy newe kw ezax.$0#$b#Vidv aslx htgxiyph wbkp Rpsbgx iro Wragv, ufwd tj ey ihafgti.$6#$b#Ovxe wzxi oy blp jyrfvz cpwsdxebw, pskx Siye, Mbtpepw, agu Ppysbe...$2#$e#S myqrv cyu gqgvph tav tpcjocm bmxp do twqp lorx, eqeib xmmvjelsnz lmpo nope.$0#$b#Kt cmede, I kpmyv ovxigxstrq wzmh osgn.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun4_2.01": "I remember some of the crazy events that happened before you came to town.$0#$b#Like what happened with George, Kent, and Shane, just as an example.$6#$b#Even some of the former residents, like Michael and Lenore...$2#$e#I think you picked the perfect time to come here, after everything died down.$0#$b#At least, I think everything died down.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun4_2.02": "S kvuixmib lfui zj tav gcldi xmmred dhtk llatonxu fpqsbe pwy newe kw ezax.$0#$b#Vidv aslx htgxiyph wbkp Rpsbgx, Opyx, tel Dsexe, ryde ks rv piewpev.$6#$b#Ovxe wzxi oy blp jyrfvz cpwsdxebw, pskx Umnseol rvh Wixokv...$2#$e#S myqrv cyu gqgvph tav tpcjocm bmxp do twqp lorx, eqeib xmmvjelsnz lmpo nope.$0#$b#Kt cmede, I kpmyv ovxigxstrq wzmh osgn.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun6.01": "I take notes of everyone here, and keep all the information I jot down on a website.$0#$b#It's pretty comprehensive if I do say so myself. It's one of the few things I've done that I'm proud of.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun6.02": "S mrsi ysdel wj pzorrfvi sibe, iro ooei ipw xre zvjzcqktbfv T nyt uway sx t eimdmde.$0#$b#St'j tcpxdy twqaciregjqzp mp B ls dei lf qjdivf. Qx'd ynx wj elo yve esmxgl Q'gp nogv xslx I'd tczyn hw.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun8.01": "Hey, you talk with the other townsfolk, right?$6#$b#I don't want to be the only person you talk to.$0#$e#You might be the only person that I can really relate to, even if it's only to a small degree.$8#$b#But at the same time, everyone else's lives are rich and interesting, even if they're not always the best people.$1#$b#I've seen a lot of their lives, and hopefully, you can see it too.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.Sun8.02": "Rer, czf daeb atel tav sesib mferdqsvk, zmrsx?$6#$b#S wfv'e aknm bs mi tav sywc pxiasy cyu kipv xy.$0#$e#Ion umrsx bx blp sxlr xicdsx myix T mag zilwpi kvteep do, mzpy sf zb'd sxlr bs l cmtct opkbex.$8#$b#Lum ix elo lrui emwe, mzpccynx mpdp'c ezdid ebe iqgs exd zvxpcictbeo, pzon zn esii'kv rze klprgw elo uvax aiypev.$1#$b#S'ov wppr a cwx zj tavqv wmfel, eyo roivnywwc, rfc nlr sxv me xyo.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_12.01": "Tomorrow is the Egg Festival, right?$6#$b#I haven't figured out how to join in there just yet. So, I'll pass on the festivities for now, unfortunately.$2#$e#But I have heard Abigail's the egg scavenging queen.$0#$b#Good luck, @! I hope you know the right path to victory.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_12_2.01": "You know, I don't think I ever asked. Did you win last year's Egg Festival?$0#$e#Well, regardless, keep on your toes, and follow your nose!$1#$b#I have drawn a map on my computer for the optimal path.$0#$b#Though, I think that map might be useless, since I think they started using different locations.$6#$b#Truth be told, I'm as surprised as you are. I think that's a new development or something.#$e#Oh well, you still can do it!$1",

  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13.01": "...? @?$3#$b#How'd you get here?...$0#$b#I'm actually super happy to see you though!$1#$q 999915 spring_13_old#But really, how did you get here?#$r 999915 250 spring_13_12#I don't know, actually.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_13#I glitched here.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_14#I used a Beach Totem.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_15#I ran as fast as I could.#$r 999915 0 spring_13_16#I came in from the forest.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13.02": "...? @?$3#$b#How'd you get here?...$0#$b#I'm actually super happy to see you though!$1#$q 999915 spring_13_old#But really, how did you get here?#$r 999915 250 spring_13_12#I don't know, actually.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_13#I glitched here.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_14#I used a Beach Totem.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_15#I ran as fast as I could.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_16#I came in from the forest.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_2.01": "...? @?$3#$b#How'd you get here?...$0#$b#I'm actually super happy to see you though!$1#$q 999915 spring_13_old#But really, how did you get here?#$r 999915 250 spring_13_12#I don't know, actually.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_13#I glitched here.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_14#I used a Beach Totem.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_15#I ran as fast as I could.#$r 999915 0 spring_13_16#I came in from the forest.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_2.02": "...? @?$3#$b#How'd you get here?...$0#$b#I'm actually super happy to see you though!$1#$q 999915 spring_13_old#But really, how did you get here?#$r 999915 250 spring_13_12#I don't know, actually.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_13#I glitched here.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_14#I used a Beach Totem.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_15#I ran as fast as I could.#$r 999915 250 spring_13_16#I came in from the forest.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_old.01": "Hope you enjoy the Egg Festival!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_12.01": "Oh really? Hmm... I'll be sure to investigate it. But you are quite the anomaly, you know that?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_13.01": "Don't say that. You'll make me blush.$8#$b#I know you're not a glitch, but I appreciate the sentiment.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_14.01": "Boo, I thought you got here through a glitch.$6#$b#Ah well, I still appreciate you stopping by regardless.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_15.01": "Ha! You'd need to run into town before 6:10 AM. That's absolutely impressive if that's true.$1#$b#@, hopefully you don't have any trouble going back.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_16.01": "Don't sell me your lies, @.$5#$b#We both know you didn't do that.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_13_16.02": "Oh. Well, you've certainly put a lot of investment to come all the way here, so you know what? I'll allow it!$1#$b#Good thing you took care of it, because I'd be pretty angry at you if you lied to me.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23.01": "If there's one thing I'm super jealous of, it would be the Flower Dance tomorrow. I can't show up there to dance.$6#$b#It's alright though, I've been around all this time, and I still dance like a slime is stuck on my leg.$0#$e#Though, it'd be nice to dance with someone...$6#$e#I wonder if Penny would be okay with sitting out for one year...$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23.02": "If there's one thing I'm super jealous of, it would be the Flower Dance tomorrow. I can't show up there to dance.$6#$b#It's alright though, I've been around all this time, and I still dance like a slime is stuck on my leg.$0#$e#Though, it'd be nice to dance with someone...$6#$b#...$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23.03": "If there's one thing I'm super jealous of, it would be the Flower Dance tomorrow. I can't show up there to dance.$6#$b#It's alright though, I've been around all this time, and I still dance like a slime is stuck on my leg.$0#$e#Though, it'd be nice to dance with someone...$6#$b#Well, you know who that someone is, but that doesn't change the fact that I can't dance with him...$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23_inlaw_Penny.01": "If there's one thing I'm super jealous of, it would be the Flower Dance tomorrow. I can't show up there to dance.$6#$b#It's alright though, I've been around all this time, and I still dance like a slime is stuck on my leg.$0#$e#Though, it'd be nice to dance with someone...$6#$e#You're going to be dancing with your wife, right @?$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23_inlaw_Sam.01": "If there's one thing I'm super jealous of, it would be the Flower Dance tomorrow. I can't show up there to dance.$6#$b#It's alright though, I've been around all this time, and I still dance like a slime is stuck on my leg.$0#$e#...I wonder if Penny is looking for a partner.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23_2.01": "*sigh* The Flower Dance is tomorrow again, isn't it? Well, I suppose it's about that time to wistfully sit in my house, and watch everyone else have fun.$2#$e#@, if you dance, just do me a favor.$6#$b#Try to find a gaudy outfit that doesn't match the rest of the dancers. If I see that, I'll know you remembered me.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23_2_inlaw_Penny.01": "*sigh* The Flower Dance is tomorrow again, isn't it? Well, I suppose it's about that time to wistfully sit in my house, and watch everyone else have fun.$2#$e#@, if you dance, just do me a favor.$6#$b#Dance with your wife in the best outfit you can find. She deserves it.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_23_2_inlaw_Sam.01": "*sigh* The Flower Dance is tomorrow again, isn't it? Well, I suppose it's about that time to wistfully sit in my house, and watch everyone else have fun.$2#$e#@, if you dance, just do me a favor.$6#$b#...$6#$e#Just have fun, alright?$13",

  "KatrielleDialogue.spring_1_2.01": "Happy New Year! Hope things go even better for you on the ol' %farm Farm, @.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon.01": "Mondays are a pretty heavy drag. Everyone's always in a bit of a slump, and frankly, I'm no exception.$6#$e#I mostly blame the humidity and the summer heat. It can get downright unbearable at times.$6#$b#The beach is nice every so often, but maybe I should have manifested in the mountains instead.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon2.01": "I could reach into the void and pull out a bunch of ice creams. It'd be pretty nice, honestly.$0#$b#Too bad I can't pull out a colder temperature for the entire town.$6#$e#Then again, you probably don't have any winter foragable seeds, do you?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon2_2.01": "I could reach into the void and pull out a bunch of ice creams. It'd be pretty nice, honestly.$0#$b#Too bad I can't pull out a colder temperature for the entire town.$6#$e#Hopefully you have a couple of winter foragable seeds saved up, right?$1#$b#...Hehe, just kidding.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon4.01": "Today's a pretty good day for a swim, but truth be told, I don't know how.$6#$b#I mean, I can surf the web, but that's about it.$1#$e#Okay, that was a terrible pun, I'm sorry. It’s not even true, I do know how to swim.$2#$b#I’ll try not to say anything like that again. Promise.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon6.01": "Hey, @. Here, have an ice cream.[233 233 233]$1#$e#Don't worry, it's on the house.$1#$b#Or, the void, I guess. It's really hot in there too, you know?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Mon8.01": "Hey, @.[233 233 233].$1#$e#What was that? Oh, just a little code I know about. Enjoy the ice cream!$1#$b#I'm watching you though, you better not name your animals after these codes, okay, @?$5#$b#@, @, @. I'm just wondering if *you're* named after a bunch of numbers.$0#$b#You'd have five items so far, just by talking to me.$6#$e#But you wouldn't cheat like that, right?$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue.01": "When I first moved in, as far as I remember, mostly everyone was here already.$0#$b#I wonder if they had to go through the same hassle I had to go through to move in.$9#$e#Then again, none of them live in the middle of the ocean!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue2.01": "I'm sometimes a very curious person, but that has definitely led to issues in the past.$0#$b#You would not believe how hard it was to inquire about anything at all!$1#$e#I'd be stuck in silence for daring to ask even a single question.$9#$b#So, if you got any questions for me, I'm all ears!$1#$e#...On second thought, maybe we’ll talk about that another day.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.01": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to take off my glasses while talking to you.$0#$b#Ta-da! Like this!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to put them back on.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$e#Sadly, it seems I can only do that when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.02": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to take off my glasses while talking to you.$0#$b#But umm... you already had me take off my glasses, so I'm gonna put them on for a second.$0#$b#Ta-da! Like this!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to take them back off.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$e#Sadly, it seems I can only do that when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.03": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to take off my glasses while talking to you.$0#$b#Ta-da! Like this!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to put them back on.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$b#Don't worry, I know you wanted me to keep my glasses on.$0#$e#Sadly, it seems I can only do that when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.04": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to wear my glasses while talking to you but...$6#$b#Ta-da! This is what you're missing!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to take them back off.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$e#Sadly, it seems I can only do that when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.05": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to take off my glasses while talking to you.$0#$b#Ta-da! Like this!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to put them back on.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$e#You know, you had me start with my glasses off, and you wanted me to put them back on?$9#$b#You're a really silly person, @.$0#$e#Anyway, it seems I can only put my glasses on and off when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue4.06": "At one point, I wanted to stick out a little bit more. Be special in my own little way, you know?$0#$e#For starters, I wanted to wear my glasses while talking to you but...$6#$b#Ta-da! This is what you're missing!$25#$b#Give me a second, I need to take them back off.$24#$e#There we go!$1#$b#Don't worry, I know you wanted me to keep my glasses off.$0#$e#Sadly, it seems I can only do that when I finish saying what I need to say, and not during it.$6#$b#Oh well, at least I can be expressive nonetheless.$1#$b#Say, here's a little something something, as thanks for listening to me ramble.$0[204 204 204]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue6.01": "I've come to realize that I'm quite talkative, way more than the other townspeople, I'd say.$6#$b#I doubt you've heard everything I got to say, but honestly, that's not a problem.$0#$b#It's usually spilling some tea about everyone, or the occasional existential crisis. Typical stuff like that.$9#$e#Oh, and Tuesdays, I usually talk about my personal favorite topic, meta!$1#$b#It's usually about the things I've gone through coming to life. It's super interesting to me, anyway. I hope you enjoy the topic too.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue8.01": "For the longest time before I had a home, I stood like a scarecrow, right next to Elliott's cabin.$0#$b#It was a pretty nice spot. Nice view of the ocean without living on it, and Elliott's piano playing wasn't bad either.$0#$e#Though I swear I could even hear Sam jamming out on his guitar.$8#$b#No offense to Elliott, I liked listening to that electric guitar more than the plinking on a piano.$0#$b#Why? I don't know, maybe it has something to do with comparisons to a well-read club president.$5#$e#Don't worry, @. In life, it's never *just* one person.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue8.02": "For the longest time before I had a home, I stood like a scarecrow, right next to Elliott's cabin.$0#$b#It was a pretty nice spot. Nice view of the ocean without living on it, and Elliott's piano playing wasn't bad either.$0#$e#Though I swear I could even hear Sam jamming out on his guitar.$8#$b#No offense to Elliott, I liked listening to that electric guitar more than the plinking on a piano.$0#$b#Why? I don't know, maybe it has something to do with the fact that I'm literally with the guitarist now?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Tue10.01": "It dawned on me that, ever since the day I met you, I've had my diary out scattered in pages.$0#$b#I accidentally had it eviscerated around the time you crossed the bridge to see me.$9#$e#I guess you might have read it, and since it's there the whole time and we're this close, I won't make a fuss about it.$0#$e#But have you checked it recently? It changes every day, though eventually it cycles over.$0#$b#I don't know why it cycles like that, but I embraced it a bit, and started throwing pages into the void, and it'd just show up there for some reason.$9#$e#Alternatively, if you don't care, that also works for me, just as well.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed.01": "I hope you don't mind me being invested in other people's lives.$0#$b#For the longest time, I didn't even consider I'd ever interact with one of them, so it felt like it wouldn't have mattered.$6#$e#Well, aside from you, anyway.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed.02": "I hope you didn't mind me being invested in other people's lives.$0#$b#For the longest time, I haven't considered I'd ever interact with one of them, so it felt like it wouldn't have mattered.$6#$e#Well, that's all out the window now. I'm glad I met everyone.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed2.01": "Elliott is a romantic, and I wouldn't call it hopeless, either.$0#$b#He's a novelist and a pianist after all, and his mouth spews flowery language.$0#$e#I think if he would ever actively search for love, he'd find it in no time.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed2_inlaw_Elliott.01": "Elliott is a romantic, and I wouldn't call it hopeless, either.$0#$b#He's a novelist and a pianist after all, and his mouth spews flowery language.$0#$e#He seems pretty happy to have found you, you know?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed4.01": "Funny, today's the only day of the week Alex doesn't go to the beach.$9#$b#From what I learned, he usually goes to Emily's house. I never took him to be interested in her...$6#$b#Maybe Haley would know.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed4_inlaw_Haley.01": "Funny, usually on Wednesdays, Alex wouldn't go to the beach and stop by Haley's house.$9#$b#I guess the saying is true, there's plenty of other fish in the sea.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed4_inlaw_Alex.01": "Funny, usually on Wednesdays, Alex would go to the beach and stop by Haley's house.$9#$b#I guess the saying is true, there's plenty of other fish in the sea.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed6.01": "I usually love watching the drama unfold in front of me, but there’s always one person I never understood: Lewis.$9#$b#I don’t understand why him not being true to his heart would jeopardize his mayoral status.$9#$e#Not like it matters, I’d wager you’d have a better standing among the community if you made that your goal, @.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed8.01": "You know how there’s a Witch living here, right?$0#$b#Apparently, she’s not evil, per say. But she has been utterly betrayed by Rasmodius. Hell hath no fury like a woman scorned, after all.$6#$b#Abigail’s also involved somehow, but to what reason, I’m not really sure. Looking at what I can see in the code, nothing is outright confirmed.$6#$e#I will say this: I’m not great with colors, but brown and green don’t make purple, you know?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed10.01": "Isn't funny how people with the largest egos tend to be the most fragile?$0#$b#Personally, I'd argue Morris would have the largest one, but he isn't the only one with that ego problem.$0#$b#Alex, for example, presents himself as a really arrogant guy, and kinda crass at times too.$9#$b#But, I seen him with his grandparents. That narcissistic exterior completely melts around them.$0#$e#It's almost cute in a way. I'm sure if someone was as close to him like his grandparents now or his mom from what I heard, you could see that side of him.$1#$b#It's a shame, honestly. Him acting sincerely is far more interesting than that whole 'machismo' schtick.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed10_inlaw_Alex.01": "Isn't funny how people with the largest egos tend to be the most fragile?$0#$b#Personally, I'd argue Morris would have the largest one, but he isn't the only one with that ego problem.$0#$b#Alex, for example, presents himself as a really arrogant guy, and kinda crass at times too.$9#$b#But, I seen him with his grandparents and with you. That narcissistic guy exterior completely melts around all of you.$1#$e#It's almost cute in a way.$13#$b#...But if that's the case, then why are we dating?$2#$b#...Hey, @. Do me a favor. Alex is a sweet guy, and he'd be gutted if you were seen dating someone else.$2#$b#It'll hurt me, but I trust you will do the right thing, for both of us and for him.$2[277 277 277]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Wed10_inlaw_Alex.02": "Isn't funny how people with the largest egos tend to be the most fragile?$0#$b#Personally, I'd argue Morris would have the largest one, but he isn't the only one with that ego problem.$0#$b#Alex, for example, presents himself as a really arrogant guy, and kinda crass at times too.$9#$b#But, I seen him with his grandparents and with you. That narcissistic exterior completely melts around all of you.$1#$e#It's almost cute in a way. I'm almost jealous that you could see that side of him so often.$1#$b#It's a shame, honestly. Him acting sincerely is far more interesting than that whole 'machismo' schtick.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu.01": "Hi @. I think you can help me out with figuring out everything.$6#$b#But I have no clue where to start...$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2.01": "Hey, @. I don’t really know anything that I can ask you to help me figure out things...$6#$q 999900/999901 null#So, do you have any questions for me?#$r 999900 10 summer_Thu2_12#What kind of things do you like?#$r 999900 10 summer_Thu2_13#Where did you come from?#$r 999901 -10 summer_Thu2_14#What color is your underwear?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2.02": "Hey, @. I don’t really know anything that I can ask you to help me figure out things...$6#$q 999900/999901 null#So, do you have any questions for me?#$r 999900 10 summer_Thu2_12#What kind of things do you like?#$r 999900 10 summer_Thu2_13#Where did you come from?#$r 999901 -50 summer_Thu2_14#What color is your underwear?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2.03": "Hi there. I’m still thinking about things, but I think I’ve made some headway. Thanks.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2.04": "Imagine thinking that asking a woman what color her undergarments are is a good idea.$6#$b#You’re unbelievable.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2_12.01": "That’s a little hard. Most items I can just create out of the code, so most things don’t have much of an appeal to me. $0#$e#But, I would have to go with Bug Steak. It’s tender like a normal steak, but gooey like a marshmallow!$1 %revealtasteKatrielle874",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2_13.01": "Hmm... I’m not sure. I’ve been here as long as I can remember.$6#$b#I could say I was stitched under the code, and you somehow undid the seams.$9#$b#That’s as far as I can really understand.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu2_14.01": "...!?$3#$b#Stay away from me, you pervert.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4.01": "Hi @! Dunno if you spoke to me when we were a little less close, but I’m taking questions today!$0#$q 999902/999903 null#Got any questions for me?#$r 999902 10 summer_Thu4_12#Why am I the only person that allowed you to finally appear?#$r 999902 10 summer_Thu4_13#What are your hopes and dreams?#$r 999903 10 summer_Thu4_14#Are you interested in anyone?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4.02": "Hi @! Dunno if you spoke to me when we were a little less close, but I’m taking questions today!$0#$q 999902/999903 null#Got any questions for me?#$r 999902 10 summer_Thu4_12#Do you think you're invisible to anyone else?#$r 999902 10 summer_Thu4_13#What are your hopes and dreams?#$r 999903 -10 summer_Thu4_14#Are you interested in anyone?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4.03": "Good morning, @! Sorry, no questions until further notice.$0#$b#It seems like you can’t ask me anything else unless you get closer to me.$0#$b#Don’t blame me, blame the code, just like what I do with all of my problems!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4.04": "Hey, @. Sorry about last time, when you asked me if I was interested in anyone.$0#$b#But just to let you know, I’m still not saying anything!$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_12.01": "Hmm... good question. The only thing that I can think of are two things.$9#$b#The first thing is the whole bridge thing, but truth be told, that’s probably not it.$9#$b#But the second thing... You’re different from everyone else here. I can say that with certainty.$9#$b#You have a little more agency than everyone else. Beyond that, I got nothing.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_12.02": "Hmm... good question.$9#$b#Well, from being with Sam, I learned how to make anyone that can't see me, well, see me.$0#$b#So, I would say there are some people that can't see me, but I can fix that situation when it calls for it.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_13.01": "Oh, a personal question!$3#$b#Well, I haven’t put much thought into it.$9#$b#I have some short term things, like maybe getting a new hobby or having fun or something.$6#$b#But as for the big picture? I got nothing, aside from surviving each and every day.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_13.02": "Oh, a personal question!$3#$b#Well, I haven’t put much thought into it.$9#$b#But, being with Sam, and seeing how everything is progressing?$8#$b#I'd say whatever those dreams and hopes are, they're on their way to being fulfilled.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_14.01": "Oh, absolutely no one in particular!$3#$b#...$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu4_14.02": "...Really?$6#$b#@, you brought me and Sam together, and that's the question you ask me?$6#$b#You know what, I'm going to pretend that you didn't ask that.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6.01": "Hey, @! Just in case you don’t know, I’m planning a little something special!$0#$b#Every Thursday in Summer, I’m taking any and all questions you have for me!$1#$b#Granted, you gotta talk to me at different closeness levels, but eh, I worked around worse limitations.$9#$q 999904/999905 null#So, any questions for me?#$r 999905 -10 summer_Thu6_12#Why do you like Sam so much?#$r 999904 10 summer_Thu6_13#How did you dye your hair?#$r 999904 10 summer_Thu6_14#How old are you?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6.02": "Hey, @! Just in case you don’t know, I’m planning a little something special!$0#$b#Every Thursday in Summer, I’m taking any and all questions you have for me!$1#$b#Granted, you gotta talk to me at different closeness levels, but eh, I worked around worse limitations.$9#$q 999904/999905 null#So, any questions for me?#$r 999905 50 summer_Thu6_12#Why do you like Sam so much?#$r 999904 10 summer_Thu6_13#How did you dye your hair?#$r 999904 10 summer_Thu6_14#How old are you?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6.03": "Hmm... All these questions, and yet I’m still no closer to figuring out everything.$6#$b#But I guess I should try to enjoy life as it comes. Maybe contemplating my own existence can happen another day.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6.04": "Sorry about before.$2#$b#Yes, I do like Sam, but... For God's sake, I get so worked up even thinking about him.$6#$b#Oh, I meant Yoba’s sake. Not God, who is God?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6_12.01": "Huh!?$3#$b#I don’t like Sam like that! Not even a little bit!$3#$b#You should mind your business, @.$5",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6_12.02": "Well, since you asked so nicely, let me tell you.$1#$b#He's cool, he's funny, he's a talented musician, a wicked skateboarder...$8#$b#He listens to me talk all the time about random stuff...$8#$b#He's kinda accident prone, but it makes him so cute!$1#$b#Oh, and he's such a wonderful older brother, since he takes such good care of Vincent.$0#$b#And...$8#$b#...I think I should stop talking. I think we'll be here all day if you let me.$1#$b#But I really do love him so, so, so much.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6_13.01": "My hair? Do you like it, @?$0#$b#You remember when you came here, and you could... you know, shuffle your appearance?$0#$b#My creative creator did something like that. She’s got an eye for aesthetics, but I might be biased on that front.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu6_14.01": "Hmm. That is a question.$6#$b#Well, metaphysically, I do recall the term 'June 9, 2021', but that doesn't really mean anything to me.$9#$b#After all, what exactly does 'June' mean? Has two thousand years passed since the beginning of time?$9#$b#However, my birthday is Summer 9. Maybe June is similar to Summer? I don't know, it's too many questions that I don't have the answer to.$9#$b#That being said, my earliest memories are roughly twenty-two years old, and typically, most folks are born anywhere between two or three years before that.$9#$b#So, I'd estimate my age is somewhere between twenty-four to twenty-five.$0#$e#Good question, it wasn't something I have considered.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8.01": "You know the deal, @.$1#$q 999906/999907 null#Got any questions for me?#$r 999906 10 summer_Thu8_12#What do you want to do in the future?#$r 999907 -10 summer_Thu8_13#What is your favorite color?#$r 999906 10 summer_Thu8_14#What color is your underwear?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8.02": "You know the deal, @.$1#$q 999906/999907 null#Got any questions for me?#$r 999906 10 summer_Thu8_12#What do you want to do in the future?#$r 999907 -10 summer_Thu8_13#What is your favorite color?#$r 999906 -100 summer_Thu8_14#What color is your underwear?",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8.03": "So, that might be the end of what I would call 'The Burning Questions of Summer.'$0#$b#But, I suppose there’s still one more round of questions, isn’t there?$8#$b#I’m sure you know how we can get there, huh?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8.04": "Oh, I never told you. Why is my favorite color neon green?$0#$b#Well, have you ever seen those crazy hacker movies like The Matrices?$0#$b#They love neon green letters and numbers for no particular reason aside from it looks cool!$1#$b#That’s it. I just think neon green looks cool.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8_14.01": "Lemme check.$0#$b#Let’s see... My underwear is navy blue!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8_14.02": "Hey, @, not cool.$6#$b#I'm... taken, okay?$2#$b#I'm sorry, but now that me and Sam are together, that's not a thing I should be answering, you know?$2#$b#...I'll forget that you asked that.$2#$b#Alright, friend?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8_12.01": "The future, huh?$9#$b#It feels like it’s a topic that comes up again and again.$9#$b#I mean, I’m content with just pursuing happiness for the rest of my life.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu8_13.01": "Really?$6#$b#We’re this close, and you don't know that my favorite color is neon green?$6#$b#I’m... rather disappointed in you, @.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.01": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_12#Do you want to get married?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to stop wearing your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.02": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 50 summer_Thu10_12#Do you want to get married?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to stop wearing your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.03": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 50 summer_Thu10_12#How is married life?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to stop wearing your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.04": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_12#Do you want to get married?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to wear your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.05": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 50 summer_Thu10_12#Do you want to get married?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to wear your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.06": "I can just tell, you want to ask me a question, right?$1#$b#@, you don't need to hesistate to ask.$0#$q 999908/999909 null#By all means, go right ahead.#$r 999908 50 summer_Thu10_12#How is married life?#$r 999908 10 summer_Thu10_13#Does pineapple belong on pizza?#$r 999909 10 summer_Thu10_14#I want you to wear your glasses from now on.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_12.01": "!?$3#$b#@, you do know that you have to, you know, upgrade your house? And give me a Mermaid Pendant?$6#$b#Well, I don't blame you for wanting to be so hasty. I want to get married too.$4#$b#But you have to follow these things. Sorry, not my rules.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_12.02": "!?$3#$b#@, absolutely, I'd love to get married!$4#$b#...I already got the mermaid pendant to give to Sam.$8#$b#But we gotta wait a little bit, you know?$1#$b#You'll see. I have something planned for sure!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_12.03": "!?$3#$b#@, absolutely, I'd love to get married!$4#$b#...I already gave the mermaid pendant to Sam.$8#$b#But we gotta wait a little bit, you know?$1#$b#You'll see. I have something planned for sure!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_12.04": "Well, @, it's everything I dreamed it'd be.$1#$b#I mean, someone that I've had feelings for since a long time came around, and now...$8#$b#It's almost too good to be true.$1#$b#I really do love Sam, @.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_13.01": "Ooh, now you want me to get into politics, by asking if pineapple belongs on pizza?$6#$b#And you waited until ten hearts too. Well, luckily, I do have the definitive answer.$0#$b#According to the code, pineapple and pizza do *not* have any special interaction, and you cannot combine them together.$9#$b#Therefore, no, pineapple does not belong on pizza.$0#$b#Lemme know if that changes though, then I'll rectify my answer.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_14.01": "Really?! First off, that's not a question.$6#$b#...But I can remove my glasses moving forward, if that's what you really want.$0#$b#See me tomorrow, @.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_14.02": "Really?! First off, that's not a question.$6#$b#...But I can keep my glasses on moving forward, if that's what you really want.$0#$b#See me tomorrow, @.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_14.03": "Really?! First off, that's not a question.$6#$b#...And you even went out of your way to select 'Always On' too...$6#$b#You can always go switch it to something else, @.$0#$b#But I'm gonna warn you, things might get a little weird.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10_14.04": "Really?! First off, that's not a question.$6#$b#...And you even went out of your way to select 'Always Off' too...$6#$b#You can always go switch it to something else, @.$0#$b#But I'm gonna warn you, things might get a little weird.$6",

  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.07": "Well, do you like how I look?$24#$b#Heh, just kidding.$0#$e#I still have my glasses on me, but I'll keep them off, just for you.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.08": "Well, do you like how I look?$24#$b#Heh, just kidding.$0#$e#I'll keep them on, just for you.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.09": "Hey, so I guess you asked all the questions you could. It was fun, wasn't it?$1#$b#Well, actually, you did miss a question, but... you wouldn't lower our relationship just to see it, right?$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Thu10.10": "Hey, so I guess you asked all the questions you could. It was fun, wasn't it?$1#$b#Hopefully you didn't torture yourself by trying to every single question in one year, right?$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri.01": "Springs have the Egg Festival and the Flower Dance. Those seem far more exciting than a Luau and the Moonlight Jellyfish.$6#$b#Watching people eat a bunch of soup isn’t that interesting, and as for the Moonlight Jellyfish?$6#$b#Well, maybe I won’t spoil it for you just yet.$0#$e#The Egg Festival and Flower Dance just has a lot more potential to have something crazy happen.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri_2.01": "Springs have the Egg Festival and the Flower Dance. Those seem far more exciting than a Luau and the Moonlight Jellyfish.$6#$b#Watching people eat a bunch of soup isn’t that interesting, and as for the Moonlight Jellyfish?$6#$b#It’s the same every single year! Even where the rare green Moonlight Jellyfish appears!$5#$b#I can’t enjoy how beautiful it is, because of how nothing changes, year after year.$2#$e#The Egg Festival and Flower Dance just has a lot more potential to have something crazy happen.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri4.01": "$d cc#You know that one perpetually tired lady that used to work in the Joja Mart?$6#$b#She's a hardcore gamer for Moonmist Acropolis, a farming game where you go mining and date people or something.$0#$e#I guess she has all the time in the world to play the game now, but I hope she’s doing well.$2|You know that one perpetually tired lady that works in the Joja Mart?$6#$b#She's a hardcore gamer for Moonmist Acropolis, a farming game where you go mining and date people or something.$0#$e#I'm pretty sure that game is good and all, but I worry about her broken sleep schedule.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri4.02": "$d cc#You know that one perpetually tired lady that used to work in the Joja Mart?$6#$b#She's a hardcore gamer for Moonmist Acropolis, a farming game where you go mining and date people or something.$0#$e#I guess she has all the time in the world to play the game now, but I hope she’s doing well.$2|You know that one perpetually tired lady that works in the Joja Mart?$6#$b#She's a hardcore gamer for Moonmist Acropolis, a farming game where you go mining and date people or something.$0#$e#I'm pretty sure that game is good and all, but I worry about her broken sleep schedule.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri2.01": "Ooh, ooh! Today’s Friday, right?$1#$b#I wonder if the cart lady’s visiting today. I sure hope so!$1#$e#I usually see her around the forest. Too bad she’s usually all business when she swings by Pelican Town.$0#$b#But trust me, I've seen her. She’s really nice when she goes home in Zuzu City.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri6.01": "Vincent and Jas are the only children living in Pelican Town.$6#$b#Occasionally, another kid shows up during a festival, and Vincent will be up front and center to be friends.$0#$b#Whether the poor kid wants to be friends with him is an entirely different question, and sadly, the answer is usually no.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri6.02": "Vincent and Jas used to be the only children living in Pelican Town.$6#$b#Occasionally, another kid shows up during a festival, and Vincent will be up front and center to be friends.$0#$b#Whether the poor kid wants to be friends with him is an entirely different question, and sadly, the answer is usually no.$2#$e#Well, I'm sure all of them will get used to hanging with Leo.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri8.01": "Before you came here, Willy had a partner named Lenore.$0#$b#She was sweet, polite, and gorgeous, basically everything he wasn’t. But, they both loved the sea.$1#$e#One day, Lenore and Willy went boating out to sea.$6#$b#And then...$6#$b#...$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Fri10.01": "Before you came here, Willy had a partner named Lenore.$0#$b#She was sweet, polite, and gorgeous, basically everything he wasn’t.$1#$b#But, they both loved the sea.$0#$e#One day, Lenore and Willy went boating out to sea.$6#$b#And then...$6#$b#...$2#$e#Well, I tried to help. But I'm not sure if I made things better or worse.$2",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat.01": "Remember that earthquake that happened this season? It was a little weird, wouldn’t you say?$0#$b#I mean, why would an earthquake reveal an entire bathhouse? I just don’t understand the reasoning why that map would appear.$9#$e#Oh, don’t mind me being lost in my own thoughts.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat_2.01": "Remember that earthquake that happened a good while ago? It was a little weird, wouldn’t you say?$0#$b#I mean, why would an earthquake reveal an entire bathhouse? I just don’t understand the reasoning why that map would appear.$9#$e#Oh, don’t mind me being lost in my own thoughts.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat2.01": "Ugh, I can't stand this heat. You'd think the void would insulate the heat, but I feel like I need an air conditioner.$2#$b#I don't know which season I do prefer, but I know which one I don't.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat4.01": "Summers feel like they're both way too long and not long enough.$6#$b#Maybe it's a store opening for the day or maybe it's a certain event you're looking for, and time inches by slower than a snail.$9#$b#But trust me, you could blink and half of your summer is gone in a flash.$0#$e#Incidentally, have you planted any Starfruits or Melons yet?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat6.01": "Every once in a while, even before I met you, I randomly get filled with loads of dread. I'm not sure why.$6#$b#I wish I knew. Such are the mysteries of existence itself.$2#$e#I'm not sure whether to think too much about it, or stop thinking about it altogether.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sat8.01": "Hey @, do you think the world revolves around me?$6#$b#Random thought, I’m aware, but there’s a lot of eccentricities that the other townspeople lack.$6#$b#I ask, because I’ve been reading some stories about characters with that type of trait. And I absolutely loathe them.$2#$e#I trust that I’m not. But if I am, you enabling me by talking to me this much certainly isn’t helping matters.$0",

  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun.01": "I’m staying home today!$1#$b#Well, I’m staying here most of every day since you did whatever you did, just to be safe.$6#$b#But it’s nice to say it out loud.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun.02": "S’u deeiigx lzxi thuic!$1#$b#Geec, T’m jbejtrq avzi xsct fn pgiby uic dmxcx gsf hsd npeepzor pwy omn, acwe xy uv wlqi.$6#$b#Lum qx’c gzki es stp me set cwyo.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun.03": "Ugh, it's about time I stepped outside of my house.$6#$b#I'm not gonna lie, I'm exhausted by going outside now, but I can't deny that being free from the fear of people is worth it.$0#$e#...Though I'll still take the opportunity to take a break at some point this week.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun.04": "Ega, me'w aufcx emwe Z weptzew wyedmne fn xj ronjm.$6#$b#S'f vse kyngr ptp, I'd iiseesmvl mj qobeo zfxciwv rzh, bnk M nex'm liyj dhtk fptrq yimi qvym kpi qikr fn apszlx qw hsbta qx.$0#$e#...Kpsfrl I'ct demvl kiop xre fxtzcxenbkg ez dadv e mvoad ix dswe gwmye dhbj appo.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun2.01": "There’s a little bit of inspiration from watching other people live their lives.$0#$b#Watching Alex work out makes me want to go exercise, and watching Leah sculpt makes me want to pick up a hobby.$1#$e#I don’t think there’s anything wrong with watching people like that, right?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun2.02": "Dhxim’w a cqxewi bbk sq mxsizzeetsx yiwq hedcazvk zxrek xizapo ezdi eloik tmgpw.$0#$b#Gamtpmyr Klxo azco onk qlvic fv alyx th os pborvzai, exd nixnsmxg Cmes wmuegb xloos dm hlrd mf ttno ui i szfly.$1#$e#S wfv’x tazvo elorx’d exymyqrr abogx atel wtkkltyk pxfxpp pskx blle, rbxpx?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun2.03": "There’s a little bit of inspiration from watching other people live their lives.$0#$b#Watching Alex work out makes me want to go exercise, and watching Leah sculpt makes me want to pick up a hobby.$1#$e#Uhh... Judging by your expression, it's probably not a good idea to be too explicit with that now, huh?$6#$b#Well, I'll just side-eye it while doing my daily rounds of walking.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun2.04": "Dhxim’w a cqxewi bbk sq mxsizzeetsx yiwq hedcazvk zxrek xizapo ezdi eloik tmgpw.$0#$b#Gamtpmyr Klxo azco onk qlvic fv alyx th os pborvzai, exd nixnsmxg Cmes wmuegb xloos dm hlrd mf ttno ui i szfly.$1#$e#Eha... Uyngbeo mj ioni iiavoslzwr, md'l xvzmellr vse e ghfl toik mf fp xyo vftwtgst nqxs xram vsh, rua?$6#$b#Geec, T'pv clax dmne-vgi tx wazti ossnz uc oeslr zsfyhc hw alwosnz.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun4.01": "It’s a lucky coincidence that the glitching that happens occurs only on Sundays.$0#$b#It’d be rather upsetting to miss out on certain events just because glitches occur for no discernable reason!$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun4.02": "St’w l vuvbg nzmxcbumrnp dhtk xsp qlbkkltyk tarb sltzegj snnybs fvpj sx Llvhljw.$0#$b#St’h mi rtkpic yzsxkbmyr do dqwd set fv npvdabe igprds acwe foctlai rpstvymw zgmuk nsc ry wzagpcrkbev vplwyn!$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun8.01": "Sunday is usually the day for a lot of religious institutions.$0#$b#I know not too many of the residents here care about that type of stuff, but I have an odd respect towards it.$0#$e#Listen, if the vastness of the code had any bit of sentience, I’d worship it night and day for my entire life.$0#$b#Yoba could be their void. Not as tangible, but in exchange, they’re given an incentive to live, and live a good life, so it might be better for all I know!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun8.02": "Cuguic tw ullipwj dhx lej jyr r pze yf imptrmyul qrdemdumzwrd.$0#$b#S dewa ysd mfw xlri hw xsp belzliyew hxim nlvo tswye xram bcap yf jbyqq, bnk M sefe rv zoh rxjxine doprzhd md.$0#$e#Vilkmr, mp mym glwdnxja zq dhx ksop raw irj fst fn dprdixeki, M’u azcwrii qx ymqhm iro hky wwv xc egkqvp psfx.$0#$b#Iour gzfpn uv xspmb ofqh. Ryt ra elrqiucm, myd be iinlknzv, esii’zi rmfeg ir trmegkqzp xy ezdi, exd cqzp e ghfl wtjo, jw te wizyb mp lemkmv qsb tct T oxop!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun10.01": "Hey, @.$2#$b#There'll come a time where you might leave this world behind. Leave *me* behind.$2#$b#It's nothing personal, I'm sure of it. But there's other things in life for you to do, you know?$13#$e#I know you're different from everyone else here. You're not the same type of entity as me, or Sam, or Lewis, or anyone.$2#$b#You popped in, seemingly out of nowhere, and unlike everyone else, I might still have reason to believe that you'll leave in the same way.$13#$e#So, I want you to know, while I still have the chance, that I do truly love you, wherever and whenever you'll be.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun10.02": "Rer.$2#$b#Dhxim'ww mofv e emwe npicp ion umrsx lxrdi elss nwvwo leazvh. Poaov *xp* bxyqro.$2#$b#St'j rzelsnz xicdsxae, M'x cukv sq md. Scx elorx'a zelor kpmyrw ig tmqp pok gsf xy wf, jzy kgfe?$13#$e#S dewa jse'kv htqjorxeb qcsw xmmvjzro xcai sibe. Gsf'vo gfb esi stdm ejto hw iyemdy ra xp, ok Aex, yr Cmatd, ok irjzro.$2#$b#Ion xsaain be, dpiwigxtc zyd hw rzhlorx, eyo enezsi pzorrfvi ppce, Q xtkrt jbmww raov vplwyn kw mppseov xslx yhl'pw poaov my xre jiqp aky.$13#$e#Co, Q hlrd rfc ez unhn, hsmve Z wetpv ardi elo vyirnp, tarb T hy micpj pyvx gsf, ghximzpc knw elpyifek gsf'pv uv.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun10.03": "Hey, @.$2#$b#There'll come a time where you might leave this world behind. Leave *us* behind.$2#$b#It's nothing personal, I'm sure of it. But there's probably other things in life for you to do, you know?$13#$e#I know you're different from everyone else here. You're not the same type of entity as me, or Sam, or Lewis, or anyone.$2#$b#You popped in, seemingly out of nowhere, and unlike everyone else, I might still have reason to believe that you'll leave in the same way.$13#$e#So, I want you to know, while I still have the chance, that all of us in Stardew Valley, we do truly love you, wherever and whenever you'll be.$1#$e#...Yes, including the people you don't like.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_Sun10.04": "Rer.$2#$b#Dhxim'ww mofv e emwe npicp ion umrsx lxrdi elss nwvwo leazvh. Poaov *fd* bxyqro.$2#$b#St'j rzelsnz xicdsxae, M'x cukv sq md. Scx elorx'a acslaucg zelor kpmyrw ig tmqp pok gsf xy wf, jzy kgfe?$13#$e#S dewa jse'kv htqjorxeb qcsw xmmvjzro xcai sibe. Gsf'vo gfb esi stdm ejto hw iyemdy ra xp, ok Aex, yr Cmatd, ok irjzro.$2#$b#Ion xsaain be, dpiwigxtc zyd hw rzhlorx, eyo enezsi pzorrfvi ppce, Q xtkrt jbmww raov vplwyn kw mppseov xslx yhl'pw poaov my xre jiqp aky.$13#$e# Co, Q hlrd rfc ez unhn, hsmve Z wetpv ardi elo vyirnp, tarb lwp oy cw tr Smrzhph Faecmc, ao wf xcfpi efdi jse, npicpzor rvh hlonxmmv jse'ec fp.$1#$e#...Pmw, mxcellmyr dhx xizapo rfc ozr't cqop.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_10.01": "Tomorrow's the Luau, huh? Color me not excited.$6#$b#The exit to my house gets blocked off whenever something happens on the beach, so I can't really leave.$2#$e#So, if you have any business with me, might as well take care of it today!$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_10_2.01": "The Luau is really odd when you think about it.$6#$b#The only reason why this whole thing happens is because Lewis wants to be Governor.$9#$e#Don't tell him, but being the Governor is based on a voting system, with places outside of Pelican Town, like Zuzu City.$0#$b#He's never gonna get that role.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_17.01": "The Luau is really odd when you think about it.$6#$b#The only reason why this whole thing happens is because Lewis wants to be Governor.$9#$e#Don't tell him, but being the Governor is based on a voting system, with places outside of Pelican Town, like Zuzu City.$0#$b#He's never gonna get that role.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_27.01": "The Moonlight Jellyfish is such a peculiar phenomenon to me.$0#$b#There's no item identifiers for them, yet they capture the interest of everyone in town.$9#$b#Aesthetics are superior to functionality with those little critters.$1#$e#Speaking of functionality, my house is closed off during the event, so I guess I probably won't be seeing you!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.summer_27_2.01": "Yup, the Moonlight Jellies are coming back tomorrow.$6#$b#I guess I'll be seeing you in the Fall!$1#$e#Say, I know they aren't actual items, but...$6#$b#Do you think they'd taste good?$8#$b#Like would they be squishy and you'd have to slurp them up to swallow them?$8#$b#Ooh ooh, or maybe they'd be a little spicy on account of being jellyfish!$8#$e#The thought of it is tantalizing, but don't worry, even if I could, I wouldn't.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon.01": "Ah, fall. The best time to wear a turtleneck sweater.$0#$e#...Hm?$6#$b#I guess I do wear a turtleneck sweater all the time, huh?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon.02": "Ah, fall. The best time to wear a turtleneck sweater.$0#$e#...Hm?$6#$b#Well, I can't find my sweater in the void, so I'll just be wearing this.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon2.01": "Lately, I've been keeping an eye at all the things I eat. I don’t think I’ve been eating anything particularly healthy.$0#$b#Having the power to literally create anything you could ever want to eat is a dangerous power to have.$0#$e#I say that, as if I haven’t been creating pizza and tacos the entire time.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon6.01": "I’ve been testing out something whenever I’m at home.$0#$b#I’ve been trying to practice how to get angry.$1#$b#It’s still a work in progress, but I think there might be a time and place for it.$1#$e#Okay, maybe it isn’t exactly 'anger', but it’s more like being able to assert myself.$0#$b#Hopefully I don’t need to use it on you!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon6.02": "So, @. I think you’ve seen me angry at this point, right?$0#$b#I hope I did a decent job at standing my ground!$1#$e#Phew, it’s a lot of hard work. I nearly fell over myself against Haley.$0#$b#Next time, I’ll be confrontational towards someone that I’m comfortable around.$1#$e#...@.$5#$b#Kidding, kidding! Hopefully you don’t give me a reason to be angry at you.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon6.03": "I managed to stand my ground, but I’ve gotten hurt anyway.$2#$b#It’s perfectly fine, @. It’s not a skill I should rely on anyway.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon8.01": "You know, Pelican Town feels like there's a divide between the supernatural and the natural.$9#$b#One the one hand, you have talking animals, and wizards, and magic and religion that has some power beyond the belief in it.$0#$b#And on the other hand, there's your farm, and science, and schooling, and marriage, and overall more mundane happenings.$0#$e#It's really just a matter of which parts of the town you cling onto more. Maybe that's why this town has a certain charm to it.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon10.01": "Oh man, I think I drank too much coffee today.$6#$b#I mean, I feel my heart going absolutely nuts. I guess it just kicked in when you spoke to me.$2#$e#...Unless, this isn't the coffee?$8#$b#@, are you making my heart flutter?$4#$b#What an interesting feeling!$1#$b#I've never felt it be this intense before, it's making me a little nervous.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Mon10.02": "Oh man, I think I drank too much coffee today.$6#$b#Once again, I was up late, as usual.$6#$e#I gotta say, these many late nights of talking are so enjoyable.$8#$b#With me and Sam laying our hearts out to each other about random things until the morning, it's really, *really* nice.$8#$b#But doing it every night? Sheesh, I'm so tired.$2",

  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue.01": "We aren't so different, you and I, @.$5#$b#In the same way you drastically altered my life, I have the potential to alter yours.$5#$e#Don't worry, that was undoubtedly a threat.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue2.01": "You know, the power to walk on water is pretty incredible, don't you think?$0#$b#Walking on something you could fall through seems more magical than... magic!$1#$e#You should definitely try it, @.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue2.02": "My house is a bit of a mess, so I hope you don’t mind it too much.$6#$b#In actuality, it took a lot of effort to get it to appear there in the first place.$0#$b#You know what they say, 'Frap!'$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue4.01": "Every so often, you'll have some special interactions with people, myself included.$0#$b#I'm just saying, those events are difficult for everyone involved, even if it's a happy occasion.$9#$e#Hey, if you ever see me walk through walls when you know I shouldn't, just let my creators know, okay?$0#$b#I want to be the best I can be.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue6.01": "My position in life was forged through trial and error.$6#$b#Where can I walk? Where can't I walk? What can I do? What do I have influence over?$9#$b#I've bumped my head into many more walls than I'm willing to admit, but I've found a couple of neat places that I can pass through.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue8.01": "@, I was wondering. Have you ever lost yourself?$6#$b#And no, I don't mean getting lost in the woods or something. I mean it more literally.$6#$b#There was one day where I was there, and not there. You know what I mean?$9#$e#At least my shadow was still there. But I was melded into the concrete!$3#$b#I wish I could tell you how that happened.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue10.01": "You hear those droning sounds in my house, right?$6#$b#It's rather ominous, wouldn't you say?$6#$b#It makes me think there should have been something done to ensure those noises aren't there.$2#$e#Well, I'm sure you can figure something out.$0#$b#You always have.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue10.02": "You remember hear those droning sounds in my house, right?$6#$b#It's rather ominous, wouldn't you say?$6#$b#You know, I've gotten more and more used to it as time went on, especially as of late.$13",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Tue10.03": "Huh, the droning sounds in my house are gone.$9#$b#I guess it goes pretty well with how I feel, huh?$1#$e#Gosh, it really does feel like a weight has been lifted over my sholders.$0#$b#And it's all thanks to you.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed.01": "It’s peculiar how things change with time.$0#$b#Relationships blossom, people age, the impending doom of Joja’s influence spreads throughout the world, it’s very interesting to watch unfold.$9#$e#Well, I don’t have any stake in any of this, so what do I care?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed2.01": "Have you been seeing the doctor over here?$0#$b#I hope he’s doing fine overall. I know the amount of work he has to do comes and goes with the seasons.$6#$e#Well, as long as you keep eating food whole, you shouldn’t ever find yourself in his clinic.$1#$b#Though, I could imagine a regular visit would be fine too. I just wish his hours were a little better.$6#$e#Incidentally, before you came here, I did try to see if he could do a checkup on someone he can't see. The answer was no.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed2_inlaw_Harvey.01": "Have you been seeing the doctor over here?$0#$b#Hah, as if I need to ask you that question, @.$1#$e#I hope he’s doing fine overall. I know the amount of work he has to do comes and goes with the seasons.$6#$b#And I hope you don’t get too lonely if he’s out for too long.$0#$b#I’d be perfectly fine if I was alone for a long, long while. But loneliness is probably not something everyone’s well-equipped for.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed4.01": "How he speaks and acts may point to the contrary, but Demetrius has his heart in the right place.$0#$b#I thoroughly believe he cares about Robin and Maru, even if he goes about it in a strange way.$0#$e#On the other hand, I don’t really have any words regarding him and Sebastian.$2#$b#I’m glad his mom and friends are in Sebastian’s life. Who knows how sheltered Sebastian would be without them?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed4_inlaw_Sebastian.01": "How he speaks and acts may point to the contrary, but Demetrius has his heart in the right place.$0#$b#I thoroughly believe he cares about Robin and Maru, even if he goes about it in a strange way.$0#$e#On the other hand, I don’t really have any words regarding him and Sebastian.$2#$b#I’m glad you, his mom and his friends are in Sebastian’s life. Who knows how sheltered Sebastian would be without you or them?$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed6.01": "Did you know that a 'Jodi', to a married soldier, means a partner that will cheat on them while they’re away?$6#$b#It’s pretty ironic for Jodi to be named that, because as far as I can tell, she’s always been faithful to her spouse.$6#$b#Indifferent to her life as a housewife, sure, but calling her a cheater is definitely inaccurate.$6#$e#Sigh... Poor woman, I hope no one gets the wrong idea when someone calls her by her name.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed6_2.01": "Did you know that a 'Jodi', to a married soldier, means a partner that will cheat on them while they’re away?$6#$b#It’s pretty ironic for Jodi to be named that, because as far as I can tell, she’s always been faithful to Kent.$6#$b#Indifferent to her life as a housewife, sure, but calling her a cheater is definitely inaccurate.$6#$e#Sigh... Poor woman, I hope no one gets the wrong idea when someone calls her by her name.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed8.01": "You know, I have heard about a tragedy that happened somewhere on the sea.$6#$b#A young child lost their parents in a shipwreck, and was subsequently raised by animals on an island somewhere.$2#$e#It's one of the few instances where I don't have a lot of information about them.$2#$b#Without a clue as to who they are or even where they are, I can't help but to feel sorry for them.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed8.02": "You know, I have heard about a tragedy that happened somewhere on the sea.$6#$b#A young child lost their parents in a shipwreck, and was subsequently raised by animals on an island somewhere.$2#$e#It's one of the few instances where I don't have a lot of information about them.$2#$b#Without a clue as to who they are or even where they are, I can't help but to feel sorry for them.$2#$e#...@.$6#$b#Please tell me that kid isn't Leo.$2#$e#...$2#$b#Your silence is deafening.$2#$b#I won't ask for any more details.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed10.01": "$d cc#Have you ever figured out why Pelican Town was in such a terrible state?$6#$b#I mean, look at the bus, or the minecarts, or even the bridge to the quarry!$3#$b#Well, it fell into disrepair because of your grandfather's death.$6#$e#He wasn't the sole person to maintain everything, but you could say he was essential to the spirit and vitality of this town.$6#$b#Well, I'm sure your grandfather would be very proud of everything you've done.|Have you ever figured out why Pelican Town is in such a terrible state?$6#$b#I mean, look at the bus, or the minecarts, or even the bridge to the quarry!$3#$b#Well, it fell into disrepair because of your grandfather's death.$6#$e#He wasn't the sole person to maintain everything, but you could say he was essential to the spirit and vitality of this town.$6#$b#Well, I leave it up to you if you want to follow in his footsteps.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Wed10.02": "Have you ever figured out why Pelican Town was in such a terrible state?$6#$b#I mean, look at the bus, or the minecarts, or even the bridge to the quarry!$3#$b#Well, it fell into disrepair because of your grandfather's death.$6#$e#He wasn't the sole person to maintain everything, but you could say he was essential to the spirit and vitality of this town.$6#$b#Well, I'm sure your grandfather would be impressed of everything you've done.$6",

  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu.01": "Hmm...$9#$e#Oh! Hello, @.$0#$e#...$9#$e#Hey, @. Why are you still talking to me? I don’t have anything interesting to say today.$6#$e#Go ahead, you probably have a lot of other things you need to do today.$1#$e#...$6#$e#Okay, I tried to be nice about it. I don’t want to interact with anyone today.$6#$e#...$6#$e#@, please stop talking to me.$5#$e#You aren’t going to get anything by continuously pestering me, you know?$6#$e#*sigh* @, you really want to bother me this much?$6#$e#We spoke eleven times today, and I still don’t have anything new to say to you!$5#$e#I wonder what would happen if I commented out my lines for today.$9#$e#Actually, that’s a pretty good idea!$0#$e#First, I’ll copy my lines and put them into the new line for today, and comment out whatever’s next.$9#$e#...And there! Try talking to me after this!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu.02": "Hmm...$9#$e#Oh! Hello, @.$0#$e#...$9#$e#Hey, @. Why are you still talking to me? I don’t have anything interesting to say today.$0#$e#Go ahead, you probably have a lot of other things you need to do today.$1#$e#...$0#$e#Okay, I tried to be nice about it. I don’t want to interact with anyone today.$0#$e#...$0#$e#@, please stop talking to me.$5#$e#You aren’t going to get anything by continuously pestering me, you know?$0#$e#*sigh* @, you really want to bother me this much?$0#$e#We spoke eleven times, not including this time, and I still don’t have anything new to say to you!$5#$e#I wonder what would happen if I commented out my lines for today.$9#$e#Actually, that’s a pretty good idea!$0#$e#I’ll find the place where my lines are, and comment out whatever’s next.$9#$e#...And there! Try talking to me after this!$1#$e#Hmm... That didn’t seem to work.$2#$e#Bear with me for a second, @. I’ll figure this out.$0#$e#Maybe I need to put a comma here, maybe that could fix it.$9#$e#...$9#$e#Nope, you’re still able to interact with me.$2#$e#I have to say, you really are dedicated to talking to me.$0#$e#Do you, by chance, have feelings towards me, @?$0#$e#If I reciprocate your feelings, would you stop?$1#$e#...$0#$e#Well, you don’t need to pull my arm. Let me confess to you and maybe you’ll leave me alone.$4#$e#@, I am deeply in love with you.$4#$e#I appreciate you talking to me so much for today.$4#$e#And...$8#$e#And...$0#$e#...$2#$e#I’m sorry, @. I can’t actually fall for someone, just like that.$2#$e#I don’t think that’s how love works. I don’t even know what love is.$2#$e#I was hoping I could just say it, and suddenly it would all make sense.$2#$e#I know I've seen everyone else say that to other people.$2#$e#Like Marnie and Shane to Jas, or Alex to his grandparents, or Robin to her husband.$2#$e#Even Willy to his fishing rod!$11#$e#I can’t just say it, @!$7#$e#Love doesn’t mean anything to me!$7#$e#It’s just something I can’t even begin to comprehend!$7#$e#Can I love something just by watching it go by?$7#$e#Every time, and I mean *every* time two people say it to each other, it’s like I’m being stabbed.$7#$e#Like getting slashed across my empty, aching chest!$7#$e#And...$2#$e#Wait, did I make a new line for the slashes to actually comment this part out?$9#$e#I didn’t!$3#$e#Hah, so that’s what the problem was!$1#$e#First, I’ll copy my lines and put them into the new line for today, and comment out whatever’s next.$9#$e#Maybe I’ll rearrange it just a little bit so it won’t look like something is missing.$9#$e#And viola! It’s perfect.$1#$e#I guess you won’t ever see these lines after all, @.$0#$e#But hey, if you do see it, and actually take the time to go through the whole thing, thank you.$1#$e#I’m not sure what love is, but I can say I appreciate the effort you’ve gone through to read this.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu4.01": "Hitting a balance of being happy with what you have and wanting to reach more is impossible.$6#$b#I literally could have anything I could ever want, but I can’t shake this feeling that there’s still something I need in my life that I don’t have.$2#$e#Sorry for getting that dark, it’s just one of those days where I’m feeling just a bit grim about things.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu4.02": "Hitting a balance of being happy with what you have and wanting to reach more is impossible.$6#$b#I literally could have anything I could ever want, but I can’t shake this feeling that there’s still something I need in my life that I don’t have.$2#$e#But still, I can't help to be happy with how things turned out.$1#$b#So, I guess I can ignore that and be happy with the relationships that I have, and the freedom I earned.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu4.03": "Hitting a balance of being happy with what you have and wanting to reach more is impossible.$6#$b#I literally could have anything I could ever want, but I can’t shake this feeling that there’s still something I need in my life that I don’t have.$2#$e#But still, I can't help to be happy with how things turned out.$1#$b#So, I guess I can ignore that and be happy with the relationship and friendships that I have.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu6.01": "You ever have that feeling that you’re not that unique?$6#$b#I mean, I have some semblance of social anxiety and have an affinity to coding like Sebastian, I play the guitar like Sam, money means nothing to me like Linus...$9#$b#I can probably go on and on, if I continue to think about it.$2#$e#Despite the fact I’m aware that I’m just a glitchy piece of code here, I feel like I’m not unique at all.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Thu8.01": "I’ve given a little bit of thought about my position here in Stardew Valley.$0#$b#I might have some similarities with some of the people here, like Shane’s existentialism, or some of Emily’s demeanor, or Jas’s awkwardness around people.$0#$b#But that doesn’t change the fact that I’m still me.$0#$b#And I’m happy about it! I am still me!$1#$e#And hey, just because people go through similar struggles or have similar traits doesn’t make them any less relatable.$0",

  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri.01": "Halfway through the first year already, huh? It feels like time flew by so fast, and so much has happened.$0#$e#Oh!$3#$b#I meant halfway through *this* year. This is your first year, not mine!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri_2.01": "Halfway through the year already, huh? It feels like time flew by so fast, and so much has happened.$0#$e#You know, I thought we would have talked a little bit more by now.$2#$b#But it’s fine by me. It almost feels like nothing’s changed for me since you did whatever you did.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri_2.02": "Halfway through the year already, huh? It feels like time flew by so fast, and so much has happened.$0#$e#You know, I thought we would have talked a little bit more by now.$2#$b#But then again, this was by choice, wasn't it, @?$1#$e#Don't worry, @, it was fun getting to know you, it'll be fun getting to know you again.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri2.01": "$d cc#That Pierre guy? He’s what I’d like to call black, decaf coffee.$5#$b#Bubble tea without boba. Hot chocolate made from water. Soda without fizz. A virgin beer. Lukewarm tea.$5#$b#He isn’t as bad as Morris, but still. I wish he was a *little* more interesting, like the rest of his family.$6#$e#I’m kinda thirsty, by the way. Couldn’t you guess?$1|That Joja Mart guy, Morris? He’s what I’d like to call a salad without dressing.$5#$b#A cheeseless pizza. Takoyaki without sauce. Fried chicken without batter. Boiled potatoes without salt. Bland as a saltine.$5#$b#Point is, he’s a very boring fellow. Can’t he talk about anything that isn’t just work?$6#$e#I’m kinda hungry, by the way. Couldn’t you guess?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri4.01": "Gus might be a good bartender, but he’s an excellent cook.$0#$e#Before you came here, he left Pelican Town for a week to compete in a cooking competition on television.$0#$b#He did pretty well for himself. Fourth place throughout the entire country is nothing to sneeze at.$1#$b#And frankly, he was fourth only because he had to make a meal he despised. I think it was Coleslaw? I could be wrong though.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri6.01": "Evelyn and Caroline were probably the closest candidates to being farmers.$0#$b#They both love flowers and they both love tending to them, and I’d say it suits them pretty well!$1#$e#I mean, old lady and gardening? Match made in heaven, and as for Caroline...?$0#$b#Well, her hair is green, so maybe that’s a sign that she’d be good with plants?$1#$b#I know there's the greenhouse in the back of their house, but the green hair, you know?$1#$e#And then of course, there’s you, @.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri8.01": "Maru's one smart cookie, don't you think @?$0#$b#Robotics, a nurse, and an assistant to her father who is a botanist, she's ridiculously smart by any measure.$0#$b#You know, it's rather odd that she lives in Pelican Town with all of her accolades.$9#$e#Well, if you're so curious, the reason is just because of her upbringing.$0#$b#Her father's parenting style leans on intellegence, and it absolutely shows.$0#$b#Though, Maru should thank her stars that she was happy with that life path.$2#$b#Makes me wonder what she would have been like if she was a carpenter instead.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri8_inlaw_Maru.01": "Maru's one smart cookie, don't you think @?$0#$b#Robotics, a nurse, and an assistant to her father who is a botanist, she's ridiculously smart by any measure.$0#$b#You know, it's rather odd that she lives in Pelican Town with all of her accolades.$9#$e#Well, I bet you're super thankful that she does, though I gotta wonder how she would have been like if she was a carpenter instead.$9#$b#Not to mention, her father raising her to be that bright, only to become a farmer's wife.$9#$b#Not knocking you for it though!$3#$b#It was her decision to marry you after all, wasn't it?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri10_inlaw_Sam.01": "From what I heard, Penny used to have a pretty massive crush on Sam in her younger years.$0#$b#I wasn't there to see it firsthand, but Pam mentioned it a couple of times to Gus.$9#$e#I'm not sure how she feels about him at this point. But I think the feelings subsided.$0#$e#...Hey, @. For no particular reason, you aren't cheating on Sam, right?$6#$e#Okay, I hate I have to do this, but here, do the right thing, @. I'd rather be hurt than you to hurt him.$2[277 277 277]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri10.01": "From what I heard, Penny used to have a pretty massive crush on Sam in her younger years.$0#$b#I wasn't there to see it firsthand, but Pam mentioned it a couple of times to Gus.$9#$e#I'm not sure how she feels about him at this point. But I think the feelings subsided.$0#$e#Well, I suppose the door isn't closed on that opportunity. They are both single after all.$0#$e#...Looking back, I find it a little funny. I pined after him all this time too.$13#$b#And now... well, you charged into my life without any remorse.$5#$e#And you're always here to check in and listen to me ramble, including now. Stop making me love you so much, @.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri10.02": "From what I heard, Penny used to have a pretty massive crush on Sam in her younger years.$0#$b#I wasn't there to see it firsthand, but Pam mentioned it a couple of times to Gus.$9#$e#I'm not sure how she feels about him at this point. But I think the feelings subsided.$0#$e#Well, I suppose the door is closed on that opportunity.$0#$b#I hope she can find someone that can bring her happiness in her life.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri10_inlaw_Penny.01": "From what I heard, Penny used to have a pretty massive crush on Sam in her younger years.$0#$b#I wasn't there to see it firsthand, but Pam mentioned it a couple of times to Gus.$9#$e#I'm not sure how she feels about him at this point. But I think the feelings subsided.$0#$e#...Hey, @. For no particular reason, you aren't cheating on Penny, right?$6#$e#She's a nice girl, and honestly, it hurts to see you be this close to me when you're married to her.$2#$b#Since I'm at the mercy of the code, I'll let you make the decision. Here.$2[277 277 277]",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Fri10_inlaw_Penny.02": "From what I heard, Penny used to have a pretty massive crush on Sam in her younger years.$0#$b#I wasn't there to see it firsthand, but Pam mentioned it a couple of times to Gus.$9#$e#I'm not sure how she feels about him at this point. But I think the feelings subsided.$0#$e#Heh, what am I saying, I know the feelings have subsided. All four of us are happily with a partner.$1#$b#Make her happy, @. She deserves the world.$0",

  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat.01": "You're the only person that can see me, right?$6#$b#If that's the case, then I think everything will be fine.$0#$e#Dealing with one person is hard enough, but any more would be a problem.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat.02": "So, turns out that you're not the only person that can see me, right?$6#$e#I wonder if there's anyone else in town that can't see me at this point.$9#$b#I probably won't know.$0",
//  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat.03": "So, turns out that you're not the only person that can see me, right?$6#$e#I wonder if there's anyone else in town that can't see me at this point.$9#$b#I think I figured out why though, so I could introduce myself and resolve that issue quickly.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat2.01": "You’ve been here a little while huh, @?$0#$b#I hope you aren’t hurting too badly with money.$0#$e#Then again, I’m not the best judge for that, am I? I’m simultaneously homeless by technicality and have incomprehensible amounts of wealth.$9#$b#Money means nothing to me, and maybe I’m free because of that. I guess Linus would know.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.01": "Hey, @. Quick question.$1#$q 999910/999911/999912/999913/999914 fall_Sat4_old#What’s your favorite thing to do in Pelican Town?#$r 999910 10 fall_Sat4_12#Talking with people#$r 999911 10 fall_Sat4_13#Maintaining a routine#$r 999912 -10 fall_Sat4_14#Making money#$r 999913 20 fall_Sat4_15#Discovering things as they come#$r 999914 10 fall_Sat4_16#I’m not sure",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.02": "Hey, @. Looks like you’re doing your favorite thing right now, huh?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.03": "Hey, @. Out of curiosity, is talking to me part of your routine?$0#$b#I’m flattered if it is.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.04": "Oh, hi @.$6#$b#Y-you’re not friends with me because I can create things out of nowhere for you to sell, right?$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.05": "Hey, @. Is this a new line of dialogue for you to see? I’d hope so!$1#$b#Just as a small heads up, there are other things I’d say but you might need another file.$9#$b#Only do that if you *really* want to. I won’t judge if you don’t.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4.06": "Hey, @. How’s your quest in figuring what you want?$6#$b#Mine’s personally going somewhere, at the pace of a stick of butter melting down a hill.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4_12.01": "I see! Well, I have been enjoying my talks with you, so that makes sense.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4_13.01": "Ahh, so the cycle of tending to your crops or fishing or whatever, day after day, is what keeps you going?$9#$b#Good to know!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4_14.01": "Oh. Well, I guess you did work in Joja for a while, huh?$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4_15.01": "Me too! I don’t know everything, but when I come across something new, it’s a flash of inspiration and intrigue.$1#$b#And to me, you’re that something I don’t know. Thanks for answering, @.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat4_16.01": "That’s perfectly fine, @. I’m that way too, and it’s not the worst thing to not know what to do.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat8.01": "You know, there's something pretty interesting about making do with what you find on the forest floor.$0#$b#I mean, you find some random Spice Berries or Leeks or Blackberries, and you can munch it up, give it as a gift, or even sell it for a small amount of money.$0#$e#I suppose that's what I'm doing with the void, after all, so I won't blame you if you do that.$0#$b#Lemme know if you manage to find a full meal on the floor! I'd be impressed!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sat10.01": "It's kinda funny how close we gotten, wouldn't you say, @?$1#$b#I'm kinda tucked away in my little corner I literally carved out for myself, and you continously go out of your way to see me.$0#$e#I mean, with all the methods of travel available in the world, like minecarts and totems and obelisks and stuff, it's still a bit of a nuisance to go to my house.$9#$b#Sure, I have those weird items in my room, but that's a little different. It's one way, so you *have* to come here first.$9",

  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun.01": "Hey @.$0#$b#S-so, how’s the weather? It’s getting c-colder, huh?$1#$e#...*sigh* I’m sorry, I’m still getting used to talking to someone.$2#$b#Please bear with me. Some days I feel pretty confident with talking, but today’s not one of those days.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun.02": "Rer.$0#$b#C-lf, sza’j xsp getkpic? St’w ridtbeo n-gylwvz, syr?$1#$e#...*amrs* I’q dsbrr, M’w lkqpw kotmzvk fwod kw elpuigx xz wymxfvi.$2#$b#Zlxrai mikr nqxs qo. Jwqp hkyl Q qpiv iimxej mogwqhpyx wbkp elpuigx, mfx thuic’c gfb zyi oy blzdi dtpa.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun2.01": "Out of curiosity, have you ever tried to catch a leaf while it’s falling?$0#$b#I could wax poetic about it, something about the cycle of life marching forward, or something to that degree.$6#$b#But in reality, it’s just kinda fun when I don’t have anything better to do.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun2.02": "Yum wj nybihjqxj, raov czf ovxi xctin mf glegr t tilq ghbcm te’l newwmxg?$0#$b#S vfcpo akx gwietg aufcx tx, lfuiesmxg rjsfe dhx kcnwi oy tmqp waktpmyr poknivo, yr jwqpelsnz bs elkt umkcpi.$6#$b#Lum qr ciklbkg, tx’j nfdx kbele qyx pymr T nog’e lkvx irjelsnz jieeib mf hz.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun4.01": "My house is what I would like to call 'a mess.'$0#$b#But it’s *my* mess, and I am proud of it!$1#$b#My proudest moment was getting my door to open.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun4.02": "Wy ywydp ss npee M whlth wmue kw nlpv 'r qpdw.'$0#$b#Lum qx’c *dg* xics, iro M af xvzfh oy qx!$1#$b#Wy gzsfoict dwqpyx wtj kpexsnz uc osyr kw zaix.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun6.01": "I've been thinking about picking up a skill. I might as well, I have infinite time and infinite resources at the tips of my fingers.$0#$b#I would say I'd learn how to program, but that's a little on the nose, wouldn't you say?$1#$e#Besides, I'm pretty sure ol’ Sebby is already a really good programmer. I don't need to squeeze into his niche.$0#$b#Maybe I should take inspiration from you, just in case I suddenly don’t have the code to pull out literally anything I want.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun6.02": "S'ov fppr tazvotyk aufcx ammkbeo fa k lbqpw. S fzole ec pvtp, M htmm tyjsnbkm etqo tel tyjsnbkm cpwyuktmw lx tav xtaw oy uc qmxgxia.$0#$b#S pfcpo wky Z'h wikrg psh xy iiwkclq, ulb esed'l i wtxdlx wr elo gfai, ayueuv'e cyu jic?$1#$e#Lelzlid, S'f xvpexi llzi zp’ Aimmc il ipcpeny r vplpvy xwso tboziiqxpv. B lsy'x nxvl ez cqnvmdp mxth pmd rscav.$0#$b#Warsm T wroncl eloo beattcedihe jczq yhl, ufwd be gldi I jchoprvy uwr’d ardi elo vfli es pnct zfx lbkmvlwpi tegxstrq B eeye.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun8.01": "I always talk about the 'void' or the 'code', but honestly, I don't have a full grasp on what it is.$0#$b#I can change certain things, I can create anything I want, and I know many things because of it.$0#$b#But the limitations are there.$6#$e#Well, I know there's a 'void' to people like the Wizard, but I'm not sure if it's the same thing.$9#$b#There are a couple of similarities, like it not having full comprehension by its expert and there being potential applications to make life easier.$9#$b#Beyond that, I probably should start calling the code 'code' and the void 'void'.$9#$e#Sorry if that got too confusing.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_Sun8.02": "S tceejd daeb emzyd mym 'gssd' wv elo 'twhp', bnk lzyictep, T hyn'k llgi a wcpw kbalg sy aram qx tw.$0#$b#S vrv nsexgx kiceesn kpmyrw, B key gbetkm lycdhbeo T aknm, eyo S dewa xexy kpmyrw bxtiydp yf zb.$0#$b#Lum blp psmbkixtzrc tim esibe.$6#$e#Geec, T oxop blpci's r 'gzmn' kw apszlx tmvp dhx Emklvn, scx T'w gfb dfvo bw me'w tav wlxi tazvk.$9#$b#Dhxim lci a twyawi oy amxtpkrbkqid, vidv me ryt yiztyk fnct nzqzrxymrdtsx up med oxivzx lrn mymvp foigx tzeixtbrt latvivrbmzyw th uevp viyv ildmor.$9#$b#Lerfvh elkt, Q acslaucg dsselw axlcx ctctmyr dhx ksop 'chum' lrn mym gzmn 'mwmo'.$9#$e#Cokig tq dhtk kze doh ksyqycigx.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_15.01": "The Stardew Valley Fair is tomorrow, and I'm stoked to see what kind of shenanigans happen!$0#$b#If there's one thing to take away with the fair, it's that orange is hot.$1#$e#Alternatively if you aren't a gambler and therefore boring, definitely try out the fishing or the slingshot challenges to earn those points.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_15_2.01": "I have something to tell you, @. I'm a really bad gambler.$6#$b#Bad in habit, and bad in execution. Don't ever bring me to a casino, I will burn everything you own.$1#$e#Maybe it's because the money doesn't mean anything to me.$9#$b#Ah well, don't follow my example if and when you go to the Stardew Valley Fair tomorrow.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_26.01": "Ooh, the night of creeping terrors and spooky monsters is almost upon us.$0#$b#Take it from me though, it feels far less interesting than it sounds.$6#$b#Halloween is just not the holiday for me, though I still think it has *some* merit to scare people.$6#$e#Sorry, not Halloween, Spirit's Eve. Been indulging in too much fictional media on the internet.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.fall_26_2.01": "@, do you enjoy being scared?$6#$b#I personally don't think it's something I'd like as a feeling, maybe from hiding so long.$6#$e#Well, if you want something scarier than Spirit's Eve, I did find something interesting in the code.$0#$b#Apparently, if you try to watch television late at night, there's a secret channel being shown today.$9#$b#But you can only see it if you made a sacrifice out of selfishness...$9#$b#Hmm. I'll leave it up to you to figure out what that means, because I sure don't know anything about it.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon.01": "Hmmm...$9#$b#Hm hm hm hm hm hm...$9#$e#...Ah!$3#$b#Sorry, @. I don’t have a lot to say today. I’m just lost in my thoughts, is all.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon2.01": "I feel a little stuck with how my life is going.$6#$b#It’s a never ending balance of trying to figure things out and enjoying myself.$6#$e#You know, even if I wasn’t some weird out-of-place entity here, I don’t think that feeling would go away.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon4.01": "You know, I'm a little scared of you being able to talk to me like this.$0#$b#But you're always coming in to check on me, and I appreciate that.$1#$e#I don't think I'll be capable of meeting anyone else. Though, I do sorta want to meet Sam.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon4.02": "You know, I'm a little scared of you being able to talk to me like this.$0#$b#But you're always coming in to check on me, and I appreciate that.$1#$e#And well, I guess I won't be talking to anyone else, so I suppose it's okay with me.$13",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon4.03": "You know, I was a little scared of you being able to talk to me like this.$0#$b#But you're always coming in to check on me, and I appreciate that.$1#$e#I wonder who I should get closer to. I do sorta want to meet Sam.$8#$b#But maybe not, I think I just get too nervous around him.$2#$b#I think I'd collapse if I got too close to him, but it's fine! There's other people in Pelican Town after all.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon4.04": "You know, I was a little scared of you being able to talk to me like this.$0#$b#But you're always coming in to check on me, and I appreciate that.$1#$e#But hey, I already introduced myself to the town and found someone really special to me so, you know.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon6.01": "@, see anything interesting on television? Like a static-filled face or something?$6#$b#My television is a little... strange, to say the very least. If you saw it, you’d know why.$6#$e#No, I don’t know why it’s like that, in case you’re wondering.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon10.01": "@, there's a little sparkle in your eyes. It's subtle, but it's there.$8#$b#I guess I noticed it at some point when we got together.$8#$e#Love, it's such an interesting feeling.$4#$b#A physiological response and an emotional response, working in tandem, to give you that fluttery feeling, that feeling of closeness.$4#$b#Beyond that? I can't explain it. And I don't think the code will help either.$0#$e#Guess the only person that can really help me understand is you, isn't it?$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Mon10.02": "@, there's a little sparkle in your eyes. It's subtle, but it's there.$0#$b#I guess I noticed it at some point when we got closer.$0#$e#Friendship, it's a feeling I always wanted to know.$8#$b#A sense of ease and trust, like I can share anything with you, regardless of how ridiculous or embarrassing I can be.$8#$b#Beyond that? I can't explain it. And I don't think the code will help either.$0#$e#I can always find it with the people I can finally meet and talk to, but there's always a bit of appreciation for you enabling any of it at all.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue.01": "The end of another year is almost here. I can’t help but look towards the past.$6#$e#Oh, how many mistakes have been made before you came here!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue2.01": "Isn’t it weird how my house is structured? You have to walk on water to get there!$0#$e#Then again, it certainly *sounds* like you’re still walking on the docks.$0#$b#Let’s ignore the fact that I wasn’t able to get that splashing sound to come out, okay?$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue4.01": "Hey, just in case I lose my memories, I want to keep this day in your mind.$0#$b#Talk to me again on a sunny Tuesday in Winter, when you have at least four hearts with me.$0#$b#And make sure you have less than eight hearts *and* it’s after I lose my memories.$0#$e#Don’t forget.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue4.02": "@...$5#$b#I know what you did.$5#$b#...$6#$b#Well, I suppose I might have asked for this. Maybe it might have been what I suggested when we were married.$2#$b#I hope I wasn’t too hurt by it, @. And I know the feeling very well, of doing things just to know what happens.$2#$b#I guess you can mark this dialogue off of the list of lines you haven’t seen in context yet, huh?$13#$b#Anyway, whether I gave you permission or not, or whether you even knew this dialogue exists, I hope you’re still willing to talk to me.$2#$b#Even though I don’t remember, I guess I might still love you after all, @.$4#$e#I guess I’ll talk to you as if we weren’t married after today, huh?$4#$b#I’ll see you around, @.$1#$e#Boy, it’d be pretty awkward if you talked to me next week on the same day and circumstance for me to say this exact spiel again.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue4.03": "@...$5#$b#I know what you did.$5#$b#...$6#$b#Well, I suppose I might have asked for this. Maybe it might have been what I suggested when we were married.$2#$b#I hope I wasn’t too hurt by it, @. And I know the feeling very well, of doing things just to know what happens.$2#$b#I guess you can mark this dialogue off of the list of lines you haven’t seen in context yet, huh?$13#$b#Anyway, whether I gave you permission or not, or whether you even knew this dialogue exists, I hope you’re still willing to talk to me.$2#$b#Even though I don’t remember, I guess I might still love you after all, @.$4#$e#I guess I’ll talk to you as if we weren’t married after today, huh?$4#$b#I’ll see you around, @.$1#$e#Boy, it’d be pretty awkward if you talked to me next week on the same day and circumstance for me to say this exact spiel again.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue8.01": "I was doing some research in the code, and I found something really interesting.$9#$b#Apparently, there are a couple of these special events that occur on the same exact day as whenever my events occur.$9#$b#But, the requirements are rather stringent, and I can't even see what type of event it is.$9#$b#I wonder what it is...$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue10.01": "There was a time when I wanted to move. Just to see what would happen if I put my room in someone else's house.$0#$b#And the world ended. Over and over and over and over again.$2#$b#It was a struggle trying to figure out what was going wrong, but it's because I forgot *one word*.$5#$e#Anyway, I managed to fix all the problems with it. That shouldn't be a concern anymore.$8#$b#Just in case you want me to move my things into your house or something, I don't know.$8",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue10.02": "There was a time when I wanted to move. Just to see what would happen if I put my room in someone else's house.$0#$b#And the world ended. Over and over and over and over again.$2#$b#It was a struggle trying to figure out what was going wrong, but it's because I forgot *one word*.$5#$e#Anyway, I managed to fix all the problems with it, but then again, that shouldn't be a concern anymore.$2",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Tue10.03": "There was a time when I wanted to move. Just to see what would happen if I put my room in someone else's house.$0#$b#And the world ended. Over and over and over and over again.$2#$b#It was a struggle trying to figure out what was going wrong, but it's because I forgot *one word*.$5#$e#Anyway, I managed to fix all the problems with it, but then again, that shouldn't be a concern anymore.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed.01": "*shiver* It’s really cold now, isn’t it?$2#$b#I wish I was able to find winter attire in the code, but I came up short.$2#$e#Then again, I guess some of the other townspeople are also freezing their butts off, so maybe it isn’t just me.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed2.01": "Leah must be freezing, huh? Living out there in the woods in her little cabin?$2#$b#It must be terribly cold. But it is admirable that she’s willing to persevere through it anyway.$6#$e#Anything for a change of scenery, right?$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed2_inlaw_Leah.01": "Before she got married to you, she’s been freezing out in the woods in her little cabin.$6#$b#Good thing you had your house repaired to accommodate a second person. Isn't that right, @?$0#$b#Makes me wonder how someone like Linus manages it though.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed4.01": "Did you know that Evelyn used to be a world-class boxer?$1#$e#...You look skeptical. You have every right to be, I was just testing to see if you’d buy anything I’d say.$6#$b#Really, what did you expect from the best grandmother in Stardew Valley?$1#$b#Seriously, she’s just a really sweet, old lady. I don’t think she has an evil bone in her body.$0#$e#Don't tell anyone, but I did catch her from falling over one time.$6#$b#She said it was a gift from Yoba she still had the strength to hold herself up.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed4.02": "That person that lives on the far side of my house, what was her name?$6#$b#Sydney, right. I wasn't able to find any information about her in the code.$6#$e#...It feels strange to not know anything about someone.$6#$b#You included, of course.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed4.03": "So, all I gathered was that Sydney's afraid of water. That's nothing in comparison to what I know to everyone else.$6#$b#@, this is how you get to meet people? This is so exhausting!$3#$e#I have to say though, it is rather refreshing to get to know someone this way.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed4.04": "Sydney seemed very confused about my house. I don't think she was comfortable walking here.$6#$b#You've never had an issue, I've never had an issue, and late nights, Abigail and Sebastian never had issues either.$0#$e#Maybe I should have a wooden plank on there, to make it look like my house belongs here.$1#$e#Still, she seemed really nice, her house disapproval notwithstanding. Hopefully I'll get a chance to know more about her.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed6.01": "Ever heard of a fellow named Mr. Qi? He’s probably the only person more enigmatic than myself, and I don’t even belong here!$0#$b#I know he isn’t a person to befriend, but rather a person to impress.$0#$b#Rumor has it, he’ll give you some snazzy things if you complete your 'life.'$9#$e#If you ask me, life isn’t something to be completed. Just go at your own pace, and make sure it’s meaningful to you.$0#$b#At the very least, that’s what I’m trying to do now.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed6.02": "...$10#$b#Mister Qi, I truly, sincerely fear him.$10#$b#I witnessed what he is capable of, and I'm nothing compared to the immense power that he wields...$10#$e#Never, ever cross him again.$2#$b#I don't want to lose you as a person in my life.",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed8.01": "I know Leah has left her old life, baggage and all, behind to pursue her dreams of being an artist.$0#$b#And Elliott arrived about a year ago to be a writer, doing the exact same thing.$9#$b#That path is terrifying to me. I've never cared to pursue a creative endeavor, especially to dedicate my life to it.$6#$b#And they can't just pick up some food out of the code like I do.$6#$e#I'd like to believe they know what they're doing, but if my life can get thrown out of balance by some nosy farmer, the future really is uncertain for everyone.$0#$e#Maybe I should have sneaked in some food for them before you came along.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed8.02": "I know Leah has left her old life, baggage and all, behind to pursue her dreams of being an artist.$0#$b#And Elliott arrived about a year ago to be a writer, doing the exact same thing.$9#$b#That path is terrifying to me. I've never cared to pursue a creative endeavor, especially to dedicate my life to it.$6#$b#And they can't just pick up some food out of the code like I do.$6#$e#I'd like to believe they know what they're doing, but if my life can get thrown out of balance by some nosy farmer, the future really is uncertain for everyone.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed8_2.01": "I know Leah has left her old life, baggage and all, behind to pursue her dreams of being an artist.$0#$b#And Elliott arrived a good while ago to be a writer, doing the exact same thing.$9#$b#That path is terrifying to me. I've never cared to pursue a creative endeavor, especially to dedicate my life to it.$6#$b#And they can't just pick up some food out of the code like I do.$6#$e#I'd like to believe they know what they're doing, but if my life can get thrown out of balance by some nosy farmer, the future really is uncertain for everyone.$0#$e#Maybe I should have sneaked in some food for them before you came along.$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed8_2.02": "I know Leah has left her old life, baggage and all, behind to pursue her dreams of being an artist.$0#$b#And Elliott arrived a good while ago to be a writer, doing the exact same thing.$9#$b#That path is terrifying to me. I've never cared to pursue a creative endeavor, especially to dedicate my life to it.$6#$b#And they can't just pick up some food out of the code like I do.$6#$e#I'd like to believe they know what they're doing, but if my life can get thrown out of balance by some nosy farmer, the future really is uncertain for everyone.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed10.01": "In terms of the second happiest couple, I'd have to give that award to George and Evelyn.$0#$b#Sure, George is a bit of a grouch, and Evelyn doesn't express too much emotionally aside from just being nice to everyone.$9#$b#But, there is no doubt in my mind that they love each other.$1#$b#No infidelity, no long distance, no familial issues, no issues, no secrets.$0#$b#Just in general, they have a very nice and happy long term relationship and marriage, through thick and thin.$1#$e#In terms of the *first* happiest couple?$8#$b#Well, it's me and you.$8#$b#I love you, @.$4",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed10.02": "In terms of the happiest couple, I'd have to give that award to George and Evelyn.$0#$b#Sure, George is a bit of a grouch, and Evelyn doesn't express too much emotionally aside from just being nice to everyone.$9#$b#But, there is no doubt in my mind that they love each other.$1#$b#No infidelity, no long distance, no familial issues, no secrets.$0#$b#Just in general, they have a very nice and happy long term relationship and marriage, through thick and thin.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Wed10.03": "In terms of the second happiest couple, I'd have to give that award to George and Evelyn.$0#$b#Sure, George is a bit of a grouch, and Evelyn doesn't express too much emotionally aside from just being nice to everyone.$9#$b#But, there is no doubt in my mind that they love each other.$1#$b#No infidelity, no long distance, no familial issues, no secrets.$0#$b#Just in general, they have a very nice and happy long term relationship and marriage, through thick and thin.$1#$e#In terms of the *first* happiest couple?$8#$b#Well, I might have two people in mind.$8#$e#By the way, thanks again for helping me introduce myself to Sam.$1",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu.01": "May I see your hand, @?$0#$b#I just want to know if there’s something about you that makes you special enough to see me.$6#$e#It’s been bothering me, you know?$2#$b#Then again, I've done that with nearly everyone in town, and I didn't see anything special with them.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu2.01": "@, I always wondered. Why did fixing that plank give you access to my house?$9#$b#Was there something there that I haven’t looked at?$9#$e#I have to admit, ever since that storm destroyed it, I was just too lazy to fix it.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu2.02": "@, I always wondered. Why did fixing that plank give you access to my house?$9#$b#Was there something there that I haven’t looked at?$9#$e#You know, ever since that storm destroyed it, I was just too lazy to fix it.$0#$b#I can walk on water, after all.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu4.01": "I learned something pretty interesting during your time here.$0#$b#Whenever I’m trying to get items from the abyss, I occasionally see your hand trying to grab something too.$3#$e#If you ever feel like you’re getting a high-five when you’re digging through your chests, that’s my way of saying 'Hello! Please get out of my house!'$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu6.01": "You used to be an office worker, right? That is something I could never even begin to imagine.$9#$b#Being confined to a small space for numerous hours, with nothing but a computer in front of your face, typing incoherent gibberish until it’s all over.$9#$b#Only for the next day to begin, to do it all over again, because you *have* to do it to survive.$9#$b#Sheesh, if that’s what I had to go through, I’d probably move here too.$2#$e#Sorry if it got a little too real. I guess there’s some perspectives I want to understand, even if I don’t envy them.$6",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Thu10.01": "@, do you ever feel like you're not acting like yourself?$9#$b#One day, you're sitting there, finally accepting of who you are.$9#$b#Maybe you see yourself as smart, or nice, or hardworking.$9#$b#Then suddenly, you do a complete U-turn and be dumb, or mean, or lazy.$6#$e#Is that true to yourself because you followed exactly what you want to do? Or the epitome of changing who you are?$9#$e#...Don't look at me, I don't know the answer to that.$0",
  
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri.01": "Sorry, @, I can’t talk much today.$6#$b#I just wanna watch what’s going on from being around the comfort of my own home.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri2.01": "The folks working at the Adventurer’s Guild, Marlon and Gil? They’re pretty close-knit.$0#$b#They’ve been through a lot of questing together, as far as I’ve seen.$1#$b#But they’re getting a little up there in age, so their adventuring has calmed down quite a bit. And it might be for the best.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri4.01": "Mr. Rasmodius is a pretty cunning wizard. He knows all about the unknown, aside from me, of course.$0#$b#Several years ago, he was able to give sentience to a little mouse, and the mouse thanked him to some degree.$0#$e#Surprised you haven’t met the little rodent. Seems like you haven’t done much around Stardew Valley.$9#$b#Honestly, it’s an achievement to not have an achievement. So good for you!$1#$e#Don’t mind me. I’m just providing light encouragement to either do something on the farm or to check your mail.$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri4.02": "Mr. Rasmodius is a pretty cunning wizard. He knows all about the unknown, aside from me, of course.$0#$b#Several years ago, he was able to give sentience to a mouse, and they thanked him to some degree.$0#$e#Just saying, if you meet the rodent, buy something from them. The wizard spends all of the money earned on food for the mouse!$1#$b#Just wished he had a better building for them, but eh, beggars can’t be choosers.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.01": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.02": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Oh wait, Krobus is a shadow being, and not ethereal? Hmm, good to know!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.03": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Oh wait, Sandy is the shopkeeper? Huh, never would have guessed!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.04": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Hmm... So you met Dwarf, but you don't know if that's his real name or not. Interesting...$9",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.05": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Oh, I see. Leo is the feral child. Should have guessed that, honestly. Thanks!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.06": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Oh wait, Krobus is a shadow being, and not ethereal? Hmm, good to know!$1#$e#Oh, and Sandy is the shopkeeper? Huh, never would have guessed!$1",
  "KatrielleDialogue.winter_Fri6.07": "You know, there’s quite a few people I have yet to meet, and I doubt I will for a long while.$6#$b#Mainly, it’s the people who don’t live here in Pelican Town or others that hide like I do. Or did, rather.$6#$b#But being who I am, I at least know of them.$0#$e#My headcanons are that Krobus is an ethereal being, Dwarf’s first name is actually Dwarf, Sandy is a feral child, and Leo is a shopkeeper.$1#$b#If I’m inaccurate about any of these, please let me know so I can adjust it accordingly.$0#$e#Oh wait, Krobus is a shadow being, and not ethereal? Hmm, good to know!$1#$e#Hmm... So, you also met Dwarf, but you don't know if that's his real name or not. Interesting...$9",
